---
// Case F — Poverty Mapping from Space.
// Spec: docs/spec-poverty-map.html (F5 dashboard anatomy, F6 design brief).
//
// Every view-model is optional. web/public/data/manifest.json says what the pipeline has
// produced; anything not yet produced renders a designed PENDING plate rather than an empty
// chart, so the page can be built and reviewed while ingest is still streaming. No number
// on this page is invented in the browser — all of them come from the pipeline's JSON.
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
---

<html lang="en" data-case="poverty" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Poverty Mapping from Space — Demo Lab</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Rooftops, night lights, land cover and population as welfare signals: a gradient-boosted small-area model trained on BPS's official regency poverty rates, spatially cross-validated, and carried down to the kecamatan." />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700;800&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to the content</a>

    <header class="topbar">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>DEMO&nbsp;LAB</a>
      <nav aria-label="Chapters">
        <a href="#ch1">01 Official</a>
        <a href="#ch2">02 Skill</a>
        <a href="#ch3">03 Signals</a>
        <a href="#ch4">04 Below the line</a>
        <a href="#explore">Explore</a>
        <a href="#method">Method</a>
        <a href="#review">Review</a>
      </nav>
      <span class="stamp" id="top-stamp">LOADING</span>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ HERO — the reveal ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section id="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-canvas-wrap">
          <div id="hero-map"></div>
          <div class="hero-veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div id="hero-wipe" class="wipe" hidden>
            <button id="wipe-handle" class="wipe-handle" aria-label="Drag to wipe between the satellite view and the inferred poverty rate" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="50" role="slider" tabindex="0">
              <span aria-hidden="true">◂ ▸</span>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-labels" id="hero-labels" hidden>
            <span class="hl left" id="hero-left-label">WHAT THE SATELLITE SEES</span>
            <span class="hl right" id="hero-right-label">WHAT IT IMPLIES</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Small-area estimation</span>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Poverty mapping<br />from space</h1>
          <p class="lede">BPS publishes a poverty rate for 514 kabupaten and kota, once a year.
          Below that line nothing official exists. But the signal is overhead: how many roofs,
          how big they are, how bright the night, how much of the ground is built.
          This case learns the relationship against every official rate from 2016 to 2025,
          tests it on provinces the model has never seen, publishes the result whichever way
          it falls, and then carries it down to the kecamatan — <em>distributing</em> the
          official number, never replacing it.</p>
          <div class="hero-ctl" id="hero-ctl" hidden>
            <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Left-hand layer">
              <button data-sees="bld_per_km2" class="on">Roofs</button>
              <button data-sees="lights_per_capita">Lights</button>
              <button data-sees="pop_density">People</button>
              <button data-sees="lc_built">Built land</button>
            </div>
            <button id="hero-replay" class="ghost">↻ Replay the reveal</button>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-note stamp" id="hero-note">PREPARING THE REVEAL…</p>
        </div>

        <div class="scroll-cue" aria-hidden="true"><span></span>SCROLL</div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ big stats ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section id="stats" class="band reveal">
        <p class="verdict" id="verdict" hidden></p>
        <div class="stat-row" id="stat-row"></div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ CH 1 ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch1" aria-labelledby="ch1-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">01</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="ch1-h">The official map, and its resolution</h2>
            <p class="lede">Every number this case is judged against comes from one place: the
            March Susenas, published by BPS as a poverty headcount for each of 514 regencies and
            cities. It is authoritative, it is annual, and it is the coarsest unit at which
            Indonesian poverty is publicly measured — a single rate for territories that run
            from 4 km² to 44,000 km².</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2 reveal">
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>The national headcount, 2016–2025</h3>
              <p class="cap">Population-weighted mean of the 514 published regency rates, and
              the band between the 10th and 90th percentile regency.</p>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart" id="trend-chart"></div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>514 regencies, one year</h3>
              <p class="cap">Every regency in the latest release, sorted. Hover for the name and
              rate; the spread is the reason a national average tells a client almost nothing.</p>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart" id="dist-chart"></div>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="sowhat reveal"><b>So what.</b> <span id="ch1-sowhat">—</span></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ CH 2 ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch2" aria-labelledby="ch2-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">02</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="ch2-h">How well it predicts — before anything else</h2>
            <p class="lede">A poverty map that has not been validated out of sample is a
            picture, not an estimate. So the trust chapter comes first. The model never sees
            the province it is scored on: 38 folds, one per province, every year of a held-out
            province removed from training. The random k-fold on the same rows is computed too
            — not as a result, but to show how much a non-spatial fold flatters a model whose
            neighbours look alike.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="gate-grid reveal" id="gate-grid"></div>

        <div class="grid-2 reveal">
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>Model against official, held-out</h3>
              <p class="cap">One dot per regency in the latest release. The diagonal is
              perfect agreement.</p>
              <div class="ctl-row">
                <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Cross-validation scheme" id="cv-seg">
                  <button data-cv="lopo" class="on">Leave-one-province-out</button>
                  <button data-cv="block">200 km blocks</button>
                  <button data-cv="random">Random k-fold</button>
                  <button data-cv="lopo_ridge">Ridge baseline</button>
                </div>
                <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Region filter" id="reg-seg">
                  <button data-reg="all" class="on">All</button>
                  <button data-reg="java">Java</button>
                  <button data-reg="off">Off-Java</button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart tall" id="scatter-chart"></div>
          </figure>
          <div class="stack">
            <figure class="card">
              <figcaption>
                <h3>What a random fold buys you</h3>
                <p class="cap">The same model and the same rows, scored under four fold
                designs. The gap between the top bar and the bottom one is the cost of
                honesty — and the size of the error a client would inherit.</p>
              </figcaption>
              <div class="chart short" id="scheme-chart"></div>
            </figure>
            <figure class="card">
              <figcaption>
                <h3>Sees forward, not just sideways</h3>
                <p class="cap">Trained on 2016–2023, then asked for releases it has never
                seen. Plotted against the strict version, where the regency's whole province
                is held out too — otherwise the model can simply remember the level it
                learned from that regency's earlier years.</p>
              </figcaption>
              <div class="chart short" id="temporal-chart"></div>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="sowhat reveal"><b>So what.</b> <span id="ch2-sowhat">—</span></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ CH 3 ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch3" aria-labelledby="ch3-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">03</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="ch3-h">What the model actually looks at</h2>
            <p class="lede">Gradient boosting is not a black box if you open it. These are the
            feature families ranked by how much they move a prediction, and below them any
            regency you pick, read back in plain words.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2 reveal">
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>Feature families</h3>
              <p class="cap" id="shap-unit">Mean absolute contribution to a regency's predicted
              poverty rate.</p>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart" id="family-chart"></div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>Read one regency back</h3>
              <p class="cap">The five signals that moved this regency furthest from the
              national average, and which way.</p>
              <label class="sr-only" for="shap-pick">Choose a regency</label>
              <select id="shap-pick" class="picker"></select>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart" id="drill-chart"></div>
            <p class="plainread" id="drill-read"></p>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="sowhat reveal"><b>So what.</b> <span id="ch3-sowhat">—</span></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ CH 4 ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter" id="ch4" aria-labelledby="ch4-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">04</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="ch4-h">Below the survey line</h2>
            <p class="lede">The payoff, and the part that needs the most care. The regency model
            is applied to kecamatan features built by the same code, then every kecamatan in a
            regency is rescaled by one factor so the population-weighted mean reproduces the
            official rate exactly. The model decides only how the official number is
            distributed inside its regency.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid-2 reveal">
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>Inside one regency</h3>
              <p class="cap">Each kecamatan with its interval; the teal line is the official
              regency rate the estimates are benchmarked to.</p>
              <label class="sr-only" for="reg-pick">Choose a regency</label>
              <select id="reg-pick" class="picker"></select>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart tall" id="interval-chart"></div>
          </figure>
          <figure class="card">
            <figcaption>
              <h3>The contrasts we can defend</h3>
              <p class="cap">Pairs of kecamatan inside a single regency whose intervals do not
              overlap — the sharpest statement this model is entitled to make.</p>
            </figcaption>
            <div class="chart" id="contrast-list"></div>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="sowhat reveal"><b>So what.</b> <span id="ch4-sowhat">—</span></p>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ EXPLORE ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter wide" id="explore" aria-labelledby="ex-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">05</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="ex-h">Explore</h2>
            <p class="lede">Official rates at the regency, model estimates at the kecamatan.
            Click any unit for its panel. The URL carries the view, so a link reopens it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="explore-ctl reveal">
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Administrative level" id="lvl-seg">
            <button data-lvl="adm2" class="on">Regency · official</button>
            <button data-lvl="adm3">Kecamatan · model estimate</button>
          </div>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="Measure" id="metric-seg">
            <button data-metric="p0" class="on">P0 headcount %</button>
            <button data-metric="p1">P1 depth</button>
            <button data-metric="p2">P2 severity</button>
            <button data-metric="line">Poverty line</button>
          </div>
          <div class="yearbox">
            <label for="year-range">Year</label>
            <input type="range" id="year-range" min="0" max="9" value="9" step="1" />
            <output id="year-out" class="data">2025</output>
          </div>
          <div class="segmented" role="group" aria-label="View" id="view-seg">
            <button data-view="map" class="on">Map</button>
            <button data-view="table">Table</button>
          </div>
          <button class="ghost" id="dl-csv">↓ CSV</button>
        </div>

        <div class="map-shell reveal">
          <div id="map" role="application" aria-label="Choropleth map of Indonesia"></div>
          <div class="legend" id="legend"></div>
          <aside class="panel" id="panel" hidden>
            <button class="panel-close" id="panel-close" aria-label="Close panel">×</button>
            <span class="stamp" id="panel-kind">REGENCY</span>
            <h3 id="panel-name">—</h3>
            <span class="stamp dim" id="panel-sub">—</span>
            <div class="panel-nums" id="panel-nums"></div>
            <div id="panel-spark"></div>
            <div id="panel-shap"></div>
          </aside>
        </div>

        <div class="table-wrap" id="table-wrap" hidden>
          <table id="data-table"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ METHOD ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter" id="method" aria-labelledby="me-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">06</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="me-h">Method, limits and provenance</h2>
            <p class="lede">Everything a reviewer needs to disagree with us.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="method-grid reveal">
          <article class="card prose">
            <h3>What is measured, and what is estimated</h3>
            <p>The target is the BPS <b>poverty headcount P0</b> — the share of people below
            the official provincial poverty line — never "wealth", never consumption. Susenas
            and DHS microdata are restricted, so the model is trained at the level BPS
            publishes and carried down from there.</p>
            <p>A regency number on this page is <b>official</b>. A kecamatan number is a
            <b>model estimate</b> with an interval, and the words and the colour differ
            wherever they appear: official series in teal, model estimates in ochre.</p>
            <h3>Benchmarking</h3>
            <p>For every regency and year, kecamatan predictions are multiplied by one factor
            so that the population-weighted mean equals the published rate. Units pinned at 0
            or 100 % hand their residual back to the units still free, so the identity holds
            exactly. The reproducibility check recomputes it from the shipped file.</p>
            <h3>Cross-validation</h3>
            <p>Leave-one-province-out, 38 folds. A held-out province leaves the training set
            in <em>every</em> year, so no temporal copy of a test regency can leak back in.
            A 200 km block scheme is reported as a spatial sensitivity, and a random k-fold
            purely to quantify its optimism.</p>
            <h3>Known limits</h3>
            <ul id="caveat-list"></ul>
          </article>

          <article class="card prose">
            <h3>Administrative-code reconciliation</h3>
            <p id="recon-summary" class="cap">—</p>
            <div class="table-scroll capped"><table id="recon-table"><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="method-grid reveal">
          <article class="card prose">
            <h3>Sources and vintages</h3>
            <div class="table-scroll">
              <table class="src">
                <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Vintage</th><th>Licence</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>BPS WebAPI — P0/P1/P2 and the poverty line, per kabupaten/kota</td><td>2016–2025, March Susenas</td><td>Free key · cite BPS</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Google Open Buildings v3 — footprints, confidence ≥ 0.70</td><td>files dated 2023-06</td><td>CC BY 4.0 (dual-licensed; CC BY elected)</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>NASA Black Marble VNP46A4 / VJ146A4 annual radiance</td><td>2012–2025, reused from the nighttime-lights case</td><td>Open (NASA) · Román et al. 2018</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>WorldPop R2025A constrained 100 m population</td><td>2016–2025</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>ESA WorldCover v200 land cover, 10 m</td><td>2021 (no later vintage exists)</td><td>CC BY 4.0</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>HDX COD-AB administrative boundaries (BPS-derived)</td><td>2020-04</td><td>CC BY-IGO</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <p class="cap">© ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel
            data (2021) processed by the ESA WorldCover consortium.</p>
            <h3>Scouted and rejected</h3>
            <p class="cap">Meta Relative Wealth Index and the SMERU 2015 poverty map are
            <b>CC BY-NC</b> and are not used, which removed the planned independent wealth
            cross-check; the temporal hold-out replaces it. BPS Podes microdata is behind
            registration and a fee. Satellite embedding sets (Tessera, Major TOM) and Open
            Buildings 2.5D Temporal are deferred on licence or size grounds.</p>
            <h3>Not in this build</h3>
            <p class="cap" id="not-in-build">GHSL built-up surface, OSM road density and
            Sentinel-2 spectral indices are specified but not ingested in this pass; each is
            additive and none of them blocks the roof / lights / population / land-cover
            families the model runs on.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card prose">
            <h3>Reproduce it</h3>
            <pre class="code">cd cases/poverty-map
uv sync
make rebuild        # ingest → features → train → downscale → validate → export
make validate       # all four published checks → data/stats.json
SCOPE=java make rebuild   # the ~11 GB fast path</pre>
            <p class="cap">Every raw input is deleted as soon as it has been reduced to
            per-kecamatan aggregates, so about 16 GB flows through a 48 GB disk that never
            holds more than a couple of gigabytes of it. The run is resumable: each completed
            unit is appended to a ledger and a rerun skips it.</p>
            <h3>Files this case publishes</h3>
            <ul class="cap" id="manifest-list"></ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══════════════════════════ REVIEW ═══════════════════════════ -->
      <section class="chapter review-cta" id="review" aria-labelledby="rv-h">
        <div class="ch-head reveal">
          <span class="chno">07</span>
          <div>
            <h2 id="rv-h">We had this case reviewed, adversarially.</h2>
            <p class="lede">An independent read of the same data against the published literature.
            It tests the defence this page used to give for its failing skill check — that the
            target is a nominal poverty line no satellite can see — by handing the model that line
            and by re-targeting it onto the line itself. Neither test supports the defence, and the
            explanation that replaces it is a better one. It also finds that night lights and
            population alone score higher than all thirty-one features, and reports what the
            benchmarked disaggregation is really worth.</p>
            <a class="cta big" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/article`}>Read the review article →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer class="foot">
      <span class="stamp dim" id="foot-stamp">A DEMO-LAB CASE · STATIC SNAPSHOT</span>
      <span class="stamp dim">SOURCE DATA: BPS · GOOGLE OPEN BUILDINGS · NASA BLACK MARBLE · WORLDPOP · ESA WORLDCOVER · HDX COD-AB</span>
    </footer>

    <div id="tooltip" class="tooltip" hidden role="status"></div>

    <script>
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      /* ── visible failure beats silent emptiness (the pattern the other cases use) ── */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div");
          b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText =
            "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;" +
            "font:13px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) =>
        failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      const sect = (name, fn) => {
        try { return fn(); }
        catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; }
      };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const DUR = reduced ? 0 : 700;

      /* ── ramps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         The poverty ramp is earth-toned on purpose: it must never be mistaken for the
         radiance ramp of the night-lights case, because lights are an INPUT here, not the
         message. Official BPS series are teal everywhere on the site; model estimates ochre;
         the raw satellite layers are a neutral steel so they read as instrument, not result. */
      const RAMP_POV = ["#1F1710", "#4A3218", "#8A5A22", "#C58B3C", "#EBD9B8"];
      const RAMP_OFF = ["#101F1D", "#173F39", "#22685E", "#39958A", "#8FD8CE"];
      const RAMP_SEE = ["#242830", "#3B434F", "#5D6774", "#8994A3", "#D6DDE6"];
      const povScale = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP_POV);
      const offScale = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP_OFF);
      const seeScale = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP_SEE);
      const OCHRE = "#D99A4E", TEAL = "#4BB8A9", MUTED = "#A99C8B", HAIR = "#332921";

      const fmt1 = d3.format(".1f"), fmt2 = d3.format(".2f"), fmtI = d3.format(",.0f");
      const fmtSI = d3.format(".3~s");
      const pp = (v) => (v == null || !isFinite(v) ? "—" : `${fmt1(v)} %`);

      /* ── shared tooltip ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      const tip = document.getElementById("tooltip");
      const showTip = (html, ev) => {
        tip.hidden = false;
        tip.innerHTML = html;
        const pad = 16, w = tip.offsetWidth, h = tip.offsetHeight;
        let x = ev.clientX + pad, y = ev.clientY + pad;
        if (x + w > innerWidth - 8) x = ev.clientX - w - pad;
        if (y + h > innerHeight - 8) y = ev.clientY - h - pad;
        tip.style.left = Math.max(8, x) + "px";
        tip.style.top = Math.max(8, y) + "px";
      };
      const hideTip = () => { tip.hidden = true; };

      /* ── designed pending / error plates ───────────────────────────────────────── */
      function plate(el, kind, title, body) {
        if (!el) return;
        el.innerHTML =
          `<div class="plate ${kind}"><span class="plate-tag">${kind === "pending" ? "PENDING" : "UNAVAILABLE"}</span>` +
          `<b>${title}</b><p>${body}</p></div>`;
      }
      const PENDING_BODY =
        "The acquisition job is still streaming this layer onto the dev server. This panel " +
        "fills in on the next pipeline run — nothing here is estimated from partial data, " +
        "because the partitions arrive in geographic order and a model fitted on half of " +
        "them would be biased, not merely noisy.";

      /* ── geometry codec (mirror of pipeline/export_web.py::_polyline) ──────────── */
      function decodePolyline(str) {
        const out = [];
        let i = 0;
        while (i < str.length) {
          let result = 0, shift = 0, b;
          do {
            b = str.charCodeAt(i++) - 63;
            result |= (b & 0x1f) << shift;
            shift += 5;
          } while (b >= 0x20);
          out.push(result & 1 ? ~(result >> 1) : result >> 1);
        }
        return out;
      }
      function buildLayer(payload) {
        const [w, s] = payload.bbox, step = payload.step;
        const units = payload.ids.map((id, i) => {
          const rings = [];
          let x0 = Infinity, y0 = Infinity, x1 = -Infinity, y1 = -Infinity;
          for (const enc of payload.shapes[i]) {
            const d = decodePolyline(enc);
            const n = d.length >> 1;
            const ring = new Float64Array(n * 2);
            let cx = 0, cy = 0;
            for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {
              cx += d[k * 2]; cy += d[k * 2 + 1];
              const lon = w + cx * step, lat = s + cy * step;
              ring[k * 2] = lon; ring[k * 2 + 1] = lat;
              if (lon < x0) x0 = lon; if (lon > x1) x1 = lon;
              if (lat < y0) y0 = lat; if (lat > y1) y1 = lat;
            }
            if (n >= 3) rings.push(ring);
          }
          return { id, name: payload.names[i], parent: payload.parents[i], rings,
                   bbox: [x0, y0, x1, y1] };
        });
        return { units, bbox: payload.bbox, res_m: payload.res_m, index: new Map(units.map((u, i) => [u.id, i])) };
      }
      // Each encoded ring becomes its own polygon: the codec flattens exteriors and holes
      // together, and treating an island as a hole would punch visible gaps in the map,
      // which is the worse of the two errors. Interior holes are rare at this scale.
      function toGeoJSON(layer) {
        return { type: "FeatureCollection", features: layer.units.map((u) => ({
          type: "Feature",
          properties: { id: u.id, name: u.name, parent: u.parent, col: "#1A1610" },
          geometry: { type: "MultiPolygon", coordinates: u.rings.map((r) => {
            const c = [];
            for (let k = 0; k < r.length; k += 2) c.push([r[k], r[k + 1]]);
            c.push([r[0], r[1]]);
            return [c];
          }) },
        })) };
      }

      /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         CanvasMap — the renderer that actually ships. The user's browser runs with WebGL
         off, so this is not a degraded path: it does hover, click, pan, zoom, hit-testing
         with Path2D + isPointInPath, and the hero's wipe compositing, which MapLibre could
         not do without two GPU layers anyway.
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
      function CanvasMap(container, opts = {}) {
        container.innerHTML = "";
        // only claim the containing block if nothing else has: the hero's map div is already
        // absolutely positioned, and overriding that collapses its height to the bitmap's.
        if (getComputedStyle(container).position === "static") container.style.position = "relative";
        const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
        canvas.style.cssText = "width:100%;height:100%;display:block;";
        canvas.tabIndex = opts.interactive === false ? -1 : 0;
        container.appendChild(canvas);
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        const hit = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d");
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);

        let layer = null, paths = [], boxes = [];
        let W = 0, H = 0, k = 1, ox = 0, oy = 0;          // projection
        let zoom = 1, panX = 0, panY = 0;                  // user transform
        let colours = [], coloursB = null, wipe = 1;
        let ground = opts.ground || "#12100C";
        let hoverIdx = -1, selected = null;

        const project = (lon, lat) => [ox + (lon - layer.bbox[0]) * k, oy - (lat - layer.bbox[1]) * k];

        function fit() {
          W = container.clientWidth; H = container.clientHeight;
          if (!W || !H || !layer) return;
          canvas.width = Math.round(W * dpr); canvas.height = Math.round(H * dpr);
          hit.canvas.width = Math.round(W); hit.canvas.height = Math.round(H);
          ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
          const [bw, bs, be, bn] = layer.bbox;
          const pad = opts.pad ?? 8;
          const base = Math.min((W - 2 * pad) / (be - bw), (H - 2 * pad) / (bn - bs));
          k = base * zoom;
          ox = (W - k * (be - bw)) / 2 + panX;
          oy = (H + k * (bn - bs)) / 2 + panY;
          buildPaths();
          bufA = bufB = null;                 // geometry moved: the cached bitmaps are stale
        }
        function buildPaths() {
          paths = []; boxes = [];
          for (const u of layer.units) {
            const p = new Path2D();
            for (const r of u.rings) {
              for (let i = 0; i < r.length; i += 2) {
                const x = ox + (r[i] - layer.bbox[0]) * k;
                const y = oy - (r[i + 1] - layer.bbox[1]) * k;
                i ? p.lineTo(x, y) : p.moveTo(x, y);
              }
              p.closePath();
            }
            paths.push(p);
            const [x0, y0] = project(u.bbox[0], u.bbox[3]);
            const [x1, y1] = project(u.bbox[2], u.bbox[1]);
            boxes.push([x0, y0, x1, y1]);
          }
        }
        // Each colour set is rendered once into an offscreen bitmap; the wipe and every
        // hover then composite bitmaps instead of re-stroking 400,000 points, which is what
        // keeps a 7,069-polygon map at 60 fps with no GPU.
        let bufA = null, bufB = null;
        function paintSet(g, cols) {
          for (let i = 0; i < paths.length; i++) {
            g.fillStyle = cols[i] || "#1A1610";
            g.fill(paths[i]);
          }
          if (opts.stroke !== false) {
            g.strokeStyle = HAIR; g.lineWidth = layer.units.length > 2000 ? 0.28 : 0.5;
            for (let i = 0; i < paths.length; i++) g.stroke(paths[i]);
          }
        }
        function buffer(cols) {
          if (!cols) return null;
          const c = document.createElement("canvas");
          c.width = canvas.width; c.height = canvas.height;
          const g = c.getContext("2d");
          g.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
          g.fillStyle = ground; g.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          paintSet(g, cols);
          return c;
        }
        function rebuild() { bufA = buffer(colours); bufB = buffer(coloursB); }
        function paint() {
          if (!layer || !W) return;
          if (!bufA) rebuild();
          ctx.save();
          ctx.fillStyle = ground; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          if (bufB && wipe < 1) {
            const x = Math.round(wipe * W);
            ctx.save(); ctx.beginPath(); ctx.rect(0, 0, x, H); ctx.clip();
            ctx.drawImage(bufA, 0, 0, W, H); ctx.restore();
            ctx.save(); ctx.beginPath(); ctx.rect(x, 0, W - x, H); ctx.clip();
            ctx.drawImage(bufB, 0, 0, W, H); ctx.restore();
            ctx.save();
            const g = ctx.createLinearGradient(x - 26, 0, x + 26, 0);
            g.addColorStop(0, "rgba(217,154,78,0)");
            g.addColorStop(0.5, "rgba(217,154,78,0.5)");
            g.addColorStop(1, "rgba(217,154,78,0)");
            ctx.fillStyle = g; ctx.fillRect(x - 26, 0, 52, H);
            ctx.strokeStyle = "rgba(240,234,225,0.85)"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.25;
            ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(x, 0); ctx.lineTo(x, H); ctx.stroke();
            ctx.restore();
          } else {
            ctx.drawImage(bufA, 0, 0, W, H);
          }
          if (hoverIdx >= 0 && paths[hoverIdx]) {
            ctx.strokeStyle = "#F0EAE1"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.6; ctx.stroke(paths[hoverIdx]);
          }
          if (selected != null) {
            const i = layer.index.get(selected);
            if (i != null && paths[i]) { ctx.strokeStyle = OCHRE; ctx.lineWidth = 2.2; ctx.stroke(paths[i]); }
          }
          ctx.restore();
        }
        function featureAt(ev) {
          const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
          const px = ev.clientX - r.left, py = ev.clientY - r.top;
          for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const b = boxes[i];
            if (px < b[0] - 1 || px > b[2] + 1 || py < b[1] - 1 || py > b[3] + 1) continue;
            if (hit.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return i;
          }
          return -1;
        }

        if (opts.interactive !== false) {
          let dragging = false, dragged = false, lx = 0, ly = 0;
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => {
            if (!opts.pannable) return;
            dragging = true; dragged = false; lx = e.clientX; ly = e.clientY;
            canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointerup", (e) => {
            if (dragging) { dragging = false; try { canvas.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {} }
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("pointermove", (e) => {
            if (dragging) {
              const dx = e.clientX - lx, dy = e.clientY - ly;
              if (Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy) > 2) dragged = true;
              panX += dx; panY += dy; lx = e.clientX; ly = e.clientY;
              fit(); paint();
              return;
            }
            const i = featureAt(e);
            if (i !== hoverIdx) { hoverIdx = i; paint(); }
            canvas.style.cursor = i >= 0 ? "pointer" : opts.pannable ? "grab" : "default";
            if (i >= 0 && opts.tip) showTip(opts.tip(layer.units[i], i), e);
            else hideTip();
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { hoverIdx = -1; hideTip(); paint(); });
          canvas.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
            if (dragged) return;
            const i = featureAt(e);
            if (i >= 0 && opts.onPick) opts.onPick(layer.units[i], i);
          });
          canvas.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
            if (!opts.pannable) return;
            const stepPx = 40;
            if (e.key === "ArrowLeft") panX += stepPx;
            else if (e.key === "ArrowRight") panX -= stepPx;
            else if (e.key === "ArrowUp") panY += stepPx;
            else if (e.key === "ArrowDown") panY -= stepPx;
            else if (e.key === "+" || e.key === "=") zoom = Math.min(zoom * 1.3, 24);
            else if (e.key === "-") zoom = Math.max(zoom / 1.3, 1);
            else if (e.key === "0") { zoom = 1; panX = panY = 0; }
            else return;
            e.preventDefault(); fit(); paint();
          });
          if (opts.pannable) {
            canvas.addEventListener("wheel", (e) => {
              e.preventDefault();
              const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
              const mx = e.clientX - r.left, my = e.clientY - r.top;
              const f = e.deltaY < 0 ? 1.16 : 1 / 1.16;
              const nz = Math.min(Math.max(zoom * f, 1), 24);
              const ratio = nz / zoom;
              panX = mx - ratio * (mx - panX); panY = my - ratio * (my - panY);
              zoom = nz;
              if (zoom === 1) { panX = 0; panY = 0; }
              fit(); paint();
            }, { passive: false });
          }
        }

        const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => { fit(); paint(); });
        ro.observe(container);

        return {
          canvas,
          // deliberately does NOT paint: every caller follows with setColours, and rendering
          // 7,069 polygons twice is the difference between a 2 s and a 5 s level switch
          setLayer(l) { layer = l; colours = new Array(l.units.length).fill(ground); coloursB = null;
            hoverIdx = -1; selected = null; bufA = bufB = null; fit(); },
          setColours(a, b = null, wipeAt = 1) { colours = a; coloursB = b; wipe = wipeAt; rebuild(); paint(); },
          setWipe(x) { wipe = x; paint(); },
          setSelected(id) { selected = id; paint(); },
          resetView() { zoom = 1; panX = 0; panY = 0; fit(); paint(); },
          zoomTo(bbox, factor = 0.82) {
            if (!layer || !W) return;
            const [bw, bs, be, bn] = layer.bbox;
            const wSpan = Math.max(bbox[2] - bbox[0], 1e-4), hSpan = Math.max(bbox[3] - bbox[1], 1e-4);
            const baseK = Math.min((W - 16) / (be - bw), (H - 16) / (bn - bs));
            zoom = Math.min(Math.max(Math.min((W * factor) / (wSpan * baseK), (H * factor) / (hSpan * baseK)), 1), 40);
            panX = 0; panY = 0; fit();
            const cx = (bbox[0] + bbox[2]) / 2, cy = (bbox[1] + bbox[3]) / 2;
            const [sx, sy] = project(cx, cy);
            panX += W / 2 - sx; panY += H / 2 - sy;
            fit(); paint();
          },
          get layer() { return layer; },
          repaint: paint,
        };
      }

      /* ══════════════════════════════════════════════ boot ══════════════════════════ */
      const j = (name) => fetch(`${base}/data/${name}`).then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null)).catch(() => null);

      const manifest = (await j("manifest.json")) || {};
      const ready = (k) => manifest[k]?.status === "ready";
      const [ledger, adm2raw, statsJson] = await Promise.all([
        j("ledger.json"), j("adm2.geo.json"), ready("stats") ? j("stats.json") : Promise.resolve(null),
      ]);
      const recon = ready("reconciliation") ? await j("reconciliation.json") : null;
      const estimates = ready("estimates") ? await j("estimates.json") : null;
      const contrasts = ready("contrasts") ? await j("contrasts.json") : null;
      const estIdx = estimates ? new Map(estimates.pcodes.map((p, i) => [p, i])) : null;

      if (!ledger || !adm2raw) {
        failBanner("Core view-models missing — run `make export` in cases/poverty-map.");
        throw new Error("no data");
      }
      const ADM2 = buildLayer(adm2raw);
      let ADM3 = null;
      const loadAdm3 = (() => {
        let p = null;
        return () => (p ||= j("adm3.geo.json").then((raw) => (ADM3 = raw ? buildLayer(raw) : null)));
      })();
      // kecamatan geometry is the hero's subject once estimates exist, so it is fetched in
      // parallel with everything else and awaited only just before the hero is composed
      if (ready("adm3_geo")) await loadAdm3();

      const YEARS = ledger.years;
      const LATEST = YEARS[YEARS.length - 1];
      const REG = ledger.regencies;
      const PROV = ledger.provinces || {};
      const codes = Object.keys(REG).sort();
      const nameOf = (c) => REG[c]?.n ?? c;
      const provOf = (c) => PROV[String(c).slice(0, 2)] ?? "";
      const yIdx = (y) => YEARS.indexOf(y);
      const val = (c, metric, y) => REG[c]?.[metric]?.[yIdx(y)] ?? null;

      document.getElementById("top-stamp").textContent =
        `BPS ${YEARS[0]}–${LATEST} · GENERATED ${ledger.vintage ?? "—"}`;
      document.getElementById("foot-stamp").textContent =
        `A DEMO-LAB CASE · STATIC SNAPSHOT · BPS RELEASE ${LATEST} · OPEN BUILDINGS v3 2023-06 · WORLDCOVER 2021 · BLACK MARBLE ANNUAL · GENERATED ${ledger.vintage ?? "—"}`;

      /* ── entrance reveals ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
      sect("reveals", () => {
        const io = new IntersectionObserver((es) => {
          for (const e of es) if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add("in"); io.unobserve(e.target); }
        }, { rootMargin: "0px 0px -12% 0px", threshold: 0.06 });
        document.querySelectorAll(".reveal").forEach((el) => (reduced ? el.classList.add("in") : io.observe(el)));
      });

      /* ══════════════════ national aggregates (from the published series only) ════ */
      const national = YEARS.map((y) => {
        let num = 0, den = 0;
        const vals = [];
        for (const c of codes) {
          const v = val(c, "p0", y);
          if (v == null) continue;
          vals.push(v);
          const w = REG[c].pop;
          if (w) { num += v * w; den += w; }
        }
        vals.sort(d3.ascending);
        return { year: y, mean: den ? num / den : d3.mean(vals), p10: d3.quantile(vals, 0.1),
                 p90: d3.quantile(vals, 0.9), min: vals[0], max: vals[vals.length - 1], n: vals.length,
                 unweighted: d3.mean(vals) };
      });
      const latestVals = codes.map((c) => ({ c, v: val(c, "p0", LATEST) })).filter((d) => d.v != null);
      latestVals.sort((a, b) => d3.ascending(a.v, b.v));

      /* ══════════════════════════════ big stats ═══════════════════════════════════ */
      sect("verdict", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("verdict");
        if (!statsJson) {
          el.hidden = false;
          el.className = "verdict pending";
          el.innerHTML = "<b>Result pending.</b> The dashboard is built; the model has not been " +
            "fitted, because the last data partitions are still landing and they land in " +
            "geographic order. No number on this page is estimated from a partial pull.";
          return;
        }
        const dec = statsJson.decomposition || {};
        const dis = statsJson.disaggregation || {};
        const s = statsJson.skill;
        el.hidden = false;
        el.className = "verdict " + (statsJson.ships ? "ok" : "fail");
        el.innerHTML = statsJson.ships
          ? `<b>All hard gates pass.</b> Held out province by province, the model reaches ` +
            `R² ${fmt2(s.lopo.r2)} and Spearman ρ ${fmt2(s.lopo.spearman)} against the official ` +
            `${statsJson.latest_year} rates, and kecamatan estimates reproduce every regency total exactly.`
          : `<b>The headline check fails, and it is published failing.</b> Held out province by ` +
            `province the model reaches R² ${fmt2(s.lopo.r2)}, ρ ${fmt2(s.lopo.spearman)} and ` +
            `RMSE ${fmt1(s.lopo.rmse)} pp, against thresholds of 0.50, 0.70 and 4.0 pp. Those ` +
            `thresholds came from studies that never held space out; a random fold on these same ` +
            `rows reports R² ${fmt2(s.random.r2)}, which is where those studies sit. ` +
            `${dec.offset_share_of_sse == null ? "Most" : d3.format(".0%")(dec.offset_share_of_sse)} ` +
            `of the squared error is a single constant offset for an entire province — the model ` +
            `pulls every regency toward the middle. Remove the offsets and it orders regencies ` +
            `inside their province at ρ ` +
            `${dec.within_province_spearman == null ? "—" : fmt2(dec.within_province_spearman)}, ` +
            `explaining R² ${dec.within_province_r2 == null ? "—" : fmt2(dec.within_province_r2)} ` +
            `of the within-province variation, across ${dec.provinces_scored ?? "—"} provinces. ` +
            (dis.benchmarked_model
              ? `Run one level up, where truth exists, the benchmarking rule this case ships beats ` +
                `giving every regency its province's rate on ` +
                `${d3.format(".0%")(dis.win_rate)} of ${fmtI(dis.n)} regencies, cutting mean error ` +
                `from ${fmt2(dis.flat_parent_rate.mae)} to ${fmt2(dis.benchmarked_model.mae)} pp. `
              : "") +
            `What ships is therefore a benchmarked <em>disaggregator</em> for exploration and ` +
            `prioritisation — not a substitute for the survey, and not a targeting instrument.`;
      });

      sect("stat row", () => {
        const row = document.getElementById("stat-row");
        const last = national[national.length - 1];
        const first = national[0];
        const lo = latestVals[0], hi = latestVals[latestVals.length - 1];
        const items = [
          { k: "official", big: pp(last.unweighted), lab: `Mean regency poverty rate, ${LATEST}`,
            sub: `${last.n} kabupaten/kota · BPS · was ${pp(first.unweighted)} in ${YEARS[0]}` },
          { k: "official", big: `${fmt1(hi.v)} %<span class="vs">vs</span>${fmt1(lo.v)} %`,
            lab: "Widest gap between two regencies",
            sub: `${nameOf(hi.c)} against ${nameOf(lo.c)} — a ${fmt1(hi.v - lo.v)} pp span the national figure hides` },
          estimates
            ? { k: "model", big: fmtI(estimates.pcodes.length), lab: "Kecamatan carrying an estimate",
                sub: `benchmarked to ${fmtI(codes.length)} official regency rates · ${LATEST}` }
            : { k: "pending", big: "—", lab: "Kecamatan carrying an estimate", sub: "waiting on the model run" },
          statsJson
            ? (() => {
                const g1 = statsJson.gates.find((g) => g.id === "G-F1");
                const dec = statsJson.decomposition || {};
                const r2 = g1.checks[0].value, rho = g1.checks[1].value;
                return { k: g1.status === "pass" ? "model" : "fail",
                  big: `R²&nbsp;${fmt2(r2)}`,
                  lab: `Held-out skill, leave-one-province-out — ${g1.status}`,
                  sub: `ρ ${fmt2(rho)} · RMSE ${fmt1(g1.checks[2].value)} pp` +
                    (dec.within_province_spearman != null
                      ? ` · inside a province, ρ ${fmt2(dec.within_province_spearman)} but R² ${fmt2(dec.within_province_r2)}`
                      : "") };
              })()
            : { k: "pending", big: "—", lab: "Held-out skill, leave-one-province-out",
                sub: "the held-out skill check runs when every partition has landed" },
        ];
        row.innerHTML = items.map((it) => `
          <div class="stat ${it.k}">
            <span class="stat-big">${it.big}</span>
            <span class="stat-lab">${it.lab}</span>
            <span class="stat-sub stamp">${it.sub}</span>
          </div>`).join("");
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════════ HERO ════════════════════════════════════════ */
      sect("hero", () => {
        const wrap = document.querySelector(".hero-canvas-wrap");
        const note = document.getElementById("hero-note");
        const heroLevel = estimates && ADM3 ? "adm3" : "adm2";
        const layer = ADM2;                        // ADM2 first paint; upgraded below if ready
        const map = CanvasMap(document.getElementById("hero-map"), {
          ground: "#0F0C09", pad: 6, stroke: false,
          tip: (u) => heroTip(u),
          onPick: (u) => { location.hash = `#c=${u.parent || u.id}`; document.getElementById("explore").scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduced ? "auto" : "smooth" }); },
        });
        // CanvasMap replaced the canvas element; keep the aria label on the new one
        map.canvas.setAttribute("aria-label", "Map of Indonesia comparing what the satellite measures with the poverty rate the model infers");
        map.setLayer(layer);

        let current = layer, sees = null, povVals = null, offVals = null;
        function heroTip(u) {
          const code = current === ADM2 ? u.id : u.parent;
          const off = val(code, "p0", LATEST);
          const est = sees && povVals ? povVals.get(u.id) : null;
          return `<b>${u.name}</b>` +
            (current === ADM3 ? `<span class="t-sub">kecamatan of ${nameOf(code)}</span>` : `<span class="t-sub">${provOf(code)}</span>`) +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Official BPS ${LATEST}</span><b class="teal">${pp(off)}</b></div>` +
            (est != null ? `<div class="t-row"><span>Model estimate</span><b class="ochre">${pp(est)}</b></div>` : "") +
            (sees ? `<div class="t-row"><span>${sees.label}</span><b>${sees.fmt(sees.get(u.id))}</b></div>` : "");
        }

        const norm = (vals) => {
          const finite = vals.filter((v) => v != null && isFinite(v));
          const lo = d3.quantile(finite.slice().sort(d3.ascending), 0.02) ?? 0;
          const hi = d3.quantile(finite.slice().sort(d3.ascending), 0.98) ?? 1;
          return (v) => (v == null || !isFinite(v) ? null : Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (v - lo) / (hi - lo || 1))));
        };

        function officialColours(lay) {
          const vals = lay.units.map((u) => val(lay === ADM2 ? u.id : u.parent, "p0", LATEST));
          const n = norm(vals);
          return vals.map((v) => (v == null ? "#1A1610" : offScale(n(v))));
        }
        function poverty(lay) {
          if (!estimates) return null;
          const key = String(LATEST);
          const idx = new Map(estimates.pcodes.map((p, i) => [p, i]));
          const arr = estimates.est[key] || [];
          const m = new Map();
          for (const u of lay.units) {
            const i = idx.get(u.id);
            m.set(u.id, i == null ? null : arr[i]);
          }
          return m;
        }
        const SEE_DEFS = {
          bld_per_km2: { label: "Building density", unit: "roofs/km²", fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : `${fmtI(v)} roofs/km²`),
                         log: true, headline: "ROOFS · GOOGLE OPEN BUILDINGS v3 · 2023" },
          lights_per_capita: { label: "Lights per person", unit: "nW·cm⁻²·sr⁻¹ per person",
                         fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : `${d3.format(".3~f")(v)} radiance/person`), log: true,
                         headline: "LIGHTS · NASA BLACK MARBLE ANNUAL · 2025" },
          pop_density: { label: "Population density", unit: "people/km²", fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : `${fmtI(v)} people/km²`),
                         log: true, headline: "PEOPLE · WORLDPOP R2025A · 100 m CONSTRAINED" },
          lc_built: { label: "Built-up share", unit: "of land", fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : d3.format(".1%")(v)),
                         log: false, headline: "LAND · ESA WORLDCOVER v200 · 2021" },
        };
        // The satellite layers are shaded by RANK, not by value. Built-up share and roof
        // density are so skewed that a linear or even log ramp collapses 90 % of the country
        // into one tone — which would be a picture of the distribution, not of the country.
        // Ranking makes each instrument legible; the tooltip always carries the real value
        // and its unit, so nothing is being hidden by the choice.
        function seeLayer(lay, keyName) {
          if (!estimates?.sees?.[keyName]) return null;
          const arr = estimates.sees[keyName];
          const raw = lay.units.map((u) => {
            const i = estIdx?.get(u.id);
            return i == null ? null : arr[i];
          });
          const order = raw.map((v, i) => [v, i]).filter(([v]) => v != null && isFinite(v))
            .sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);
          const rank = new Array(raw.length).fill(null);
          order.forEach(([, i], k) => { rank[i] = order.length > 1 ? k / (order.length - 1) : 0.5; });
          const byId = new Map(lay.units.map((u, i) => [u.id, raw[i]]));
          return { ...SEE_DEFS[keyName], get: (id) => byId.get(id),
                   colours: rank.map((t) => (t == null ? "#16181C" : seeScale(Math.pow(t, 0.9)))) };
        }

        /* ---- pending state: BPS official only, plate on the model half ---- */
        if (!estimates) {
          current = ADM2;
          offVals = officialColours(ADM2);
          map.setColours(offVals);
          note.textContent = `OFFICIAL BPS ${LATEST} · 514 REGENCIES · MODEL SURFACE PENDING`;
          const el = document.createElement("div");
          el.className = "hero-pending";
          // appended to the section, not the canvas frame, so it can drop below the map
          // on a narrow screen instead of covering it
          document.getElementById("hero").insertBefore(el, wrap.nextSibling);
          el.innerHTML =
            `<span class="plate-tag">PENDING</span><b>The reveal turns on when the last partition lands.</b>` +
            `<p>The satellite layers and the inferred poverty surface are computed from ` +
            `Open Buildings, Black Marble, WorldPop and WorldCover, which are still streaming ` +
            `onto the dev server. Until then this map shows the official BPS regency rate only — ` +
            `the ground truth the model will be judged against.</p>`;
          return;
        }

        /* ---- full reveal ---- */
        const useLay = ADM3 || ADM2;
        current = useLay;
        map.setLayer(useLay);
        povVals = poverty(useLay);
        const povNorm = norm([...povVals.values()]);
        const povColours = useLay.units.map((u) => {
          const v = povVals.get(u.id);
          return v == null ? "#1A1610" : povScale(povNorm(v));
        });
        offVals = officialColours(useLay);

        let seeKey = "bld_per_km2";
        sees = seeLayer(useLay, seeKey);
        let rightState = "model";

        document.getElementById("hero-ctl").hidden = false;
        document.getElementById("hero-labels").hidden = false;
        document.getElementById("hero-wipe").hidden = false;

        const wipeEl = document.getElementById("hero-wipe");
        const handle = document.getElementById("wipe-handle");
        let wipeAt = 0.46;
        const applyWipe = () => {
          map.setColours(sees ? sees.colours : offVals,
                         rightState === "model" ? povColours : offVals, wipeAt);
          handle.style.left = `${wipeAt * 100}%`;
          handle.setAttribute("aria-valuenow", Math.round(wipeAt * 100));
        };
        const setSee = (keyName) => {
          seeKey = keyName;
          sees = seeLayer(useLay, keyName);
          document.getElementById("hero-left-label").textContent = sees ? sees.headline : "WHAT THE SATELLITE SEES";
          note.textContent = `${useLay.units.length.toLocaleString()} KECAMATAN · ${sees ? sees.headline : ""} · MODEL ESTIMATE BENCHMARKED TO BPS ${LATEST}`;
          applyWipe();
        };
        document.querySelectorAll("#hero-ctl [data-sees]").forEach((b) =>
          b.addEventListener("click", () => {
            document.querySelectorAll("#hero-ctl [data-sees]").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
            setSee(b.dataset.sees);
          }));

        const setWipeFromClientX = (cx) => {
          const r = wipeEl.getBoundingClientRect();
          wipeAt = Math.max(0.02, Math.min(0.98, (cx - r.left) / r.width));
          applyWipe();
        };
        let dragging = false;
        handle.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => { dragging = true; handle.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); e.preventDefault(); });
        handle.addEventListener("pointermove", (e) => { if (dragging) setWipeFromClientX(e.clientX); });
        handle.addEventListener("pointerup", (e) => { dragging = false; try { handle.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {} });
        wipeEl.addEventListener("pointerdown", (e) => { if (e.target === wipeEl) setWipeFromClientX(e.clientX); });
        handle.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
          const d = e.key === "ArrowLeft" ? -0.04 : e.key === "ArrowRight" ? 0.04 : 0;
          if (!d) return;
          e.preventDefault();
          wipeAt = Math.max(0.02, Math.min(0.98, wipeAt + d));
          applyWipe();
        });

        /* the orchestrated moment: layers arrive one at a time, then collapse into the
           inferred surface. Pre-composited colour arrays, crossfaded — no per-frame
           geometry work, so it stays smooth on 7,069 polygons without a GPU. */
        function crossfade(fromCols, toCols, ms, onDone) {
          if (reduced || ms === 0) { map.setColours(toCols); onDone?.(); return; }
          const t0 = performance.now();
          const mix = new Array(toCols.length);
          // interpolators built once, not once per element per frame
          const interp = toCols.map((c, i) => d3.interpolateRgb(fromCols[i] ?? "#0F0C09", c));
          const step = (now) => {
            const t = Math.min(1, (now - t0) / ms);
            const e = t < 0.5 ? 2 * t * t : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * t + 2, 2) / 2;
            for (let i = 0; i < toCols.length; i++) mix[i] = interp[i](e);
            map.setColours(mix);
            if (t < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step); else onDone?.();
          };
          requestAnimationFrame(step);
        }
        const order = ["bld_per_km2", "lights_per_capita", "pop_density", "lc_built"];
        let introTimer = null;
        function runIntro() {
          clearTimeout(introTimer);
          document.getElementById("hero-wipe").hidden = true;
          const frames = order.map((keyName) => seeLayer(useLay, keyName)).filter(Boolean);
          if (!frames.length) { setSee(seeKey); document.getElementById("hero-wipe").hidden = false; return; }
          let i = 0;
          let prev = new Array(useLay.units.length).fill("#0F0C09");
          const next = () => {
            if (i >= frames.length) {
              note.textContent = "COLLAPSING THE LAYERS INTO ONE INFERRED SURFACE…";
              crossfade(prev, povColours, reduced ? 0 : 1100, () => {
                document.getElementById("hero-wipe").hidden = false;
                setSee(order[0]);
                document.querySelectorAll("#hero-ctl [data-sees]").forEach((x) =>
                  x.classList.toggle("on", x.dataset.sees === order[0]));
              });
              return;
            }
            const f = frames[i];
            note.textContent = f.headline;
            document.getElementById("hero-left-label").textContent = f.headline;
            crossfade(prev, f.colours, reduced ? 0 : 620, () => {
              prev = f.colours; i++;
              introTimer = setTimeout(next, reduced ? 0 : 620);
            });
          };
          next();
        }
        document.getElementById("hero-replay").addEventListener("click", runIntro);

        if (reduced) { setSee(seeKey); }
        else {
          const io = new IntersectionObserver((es) => {
            if (es.some((e) => e.isIntersecting)) { io.disconnect(); runIntro(); }
          }, { threshold: 0.25 });
          io.observe(wrap);
        }
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ CH1 charts ═════════════════════════════════════ */
      const axisStyle = (g) => g.selectAll("text").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED)
        .attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace");

      sect("trend chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("trend-chart");
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 250, M = { t: 14, r: 16, b: 30, l: 44 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img")
          .attr("aria-label", "National poverty headcount 2016 to 2025 with the 10th to 90th percentile band");
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([YEARS[0], LATEST], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(national, (d) => d.p90) * 1.12], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const defs = svg.append("defs");
        const grad = defs.append("linearGradient").attr("id", "bandg").attr("x1", 0).attr("y1", 0).attr("x2", 0).attr("y2", 1);
        grad.append("stop").attr("offset", "0%").attr("stop-color", TEAL).attr("stop-opacity", 0.26);
        grad.append("stop").attr("offset", "100%").attr("stop-color", TEAL).attr("stop-opacity", 0.03);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(5).tickFormat(d3.format("d")).tickSizeOuter(0)).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSize(-(W - M.l - M.r)))
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("line").attr("stroke", HAIR))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove()).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("path").datum(national)
          .attr("fill", "url(#bandg)")
          .attr("d", d3.area().x((d) => x(d.year)).y0((d) => y(d.p10)).y1((d) => y(d.p90)).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX));
        const line = d3.line().x((d) => x(d.year)).y((d) => y(d.unweighted)).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX);
        const path = svg.append("path").datum(national).attr("fill", "none")
          .attr("stroke", TEAL).attr("stroke-width", 2.2).attr("d", line);
        const len = path.node().getTotalLength();
        if (!reduced) path.attr("stroke-dasharray", `${len} ${len}`).attr("stroke-dashoffset", len)
          .transition().duration(DUR * 1.4).ease(d3.easeCubicOut).attr("stroke-dashoffset", 0);
        svg.selectAll("circle.pt").data(national).join("circle").attr("class", "pt")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.year)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.unweighted)).attr("r", 3.4)
          .attr("fill", "#14100C").attr("stroke", TEAL).attr("stroke-width", 1.6);
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b)
          .attr("stroke", "#F0EAE1").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.35).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r)
          .attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const [px] = d3.pointer(e);
            const d = national.reduce((b, s) => (Math.abs(x(s.year) - px) < Math.abs(x(b.year) - px) ? s : b), national[0]);
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(d.year)).attr("x2", x(d.year));
            showTip(`<b>${d.year}</b><div class="t-row"><span>Mean regency rate</span><b class="teal">${pp(d.unweighted)}</b></div>` +
              `<div class="t-row"><span>Population-weighted</span><b class="teal">${pp(d.mean)}</b></div>` +
              `<div class="t-row"><span>10th–90th percentile</span><b>${pp(d.p10)} – ${pp(d.p90)}</b></div>` +
              `<div class="t-row"><span>Regencies reporting</span><b>${d.n}</b></div>`, e);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); hideTip(); });
      });

      sect("distribution chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("dist-chart");
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 250, M = { t: 14, r: 16, b: 30, l: 44 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img")
          .attr("aria-label", `All ${latestVals.length} regency poverty rates for ${LATEST}, sorted`);
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, latestVals.length - 1], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(latestVals, (d) => d.v) * 1.08], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(4).tickFormat((v) => `#${Math.round(v) + 1}`).tickSizeOuter(0)).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(5).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSize(-(W - M.l - M.r)))
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("line").attr("stroke", HAIR))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove()).call(axisStyle);
        const bw = Math.max(1, (W - M.l - M.r) / latestVals.length - 0.6);
        const bars = svg.selectAll("rect.b").data(latestVals).join("rect").attr("class", "b")
          .attr("x", (d, i) => x(i)).attr("width", bw)
          .attr("y", H - M.b).attr("height", 0)
          .attr("fill", (d) => offScale(0.25 + 0.7 * (d.v / latestVals[latestVals.length - 1].v)));
        bars.transition().duration(DUR).delay((d, i) => (reduced ? 0 : i * 0.7))
          .attr("y", (d) => y(d.v)).attr("height", (d) => H - M.b - y(d.v));
        const meanY = y(national[national.length - 1].unweighted);
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", M.l).attr("x2", W - M.r).attr("y1", meanY).attr("y2", meanY)
          .attr("stroke", "#F0EAE1").attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 3").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.5);
        svg.append("text").attr("x", M.l + 8).attr("y", meanY - 7)
          .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
          .text(`mean of the 514 ${pp(national[national.length - 1].unweighted)}`);
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r)
          .attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const [px] = d3.pointer(e);
            const i = Math.max(0, Math.min(latestVals.length - 1, Math.round(x.invert(px))));
            const d = latestVals[i];
            bars.attr("opacity", (_, k) => (k === i ? 1 : 0.55));
            showTip(`<b>${nameOf(d.c)}</b><span class="t-sub">${provOf(d.c)} · rank ${i + 1} of ${latestVals.length}</span>` +
              `<div class="t-row"><span>P0 headcount ${LATEST}</span><b class="teal">${pp(d.v)}</b></div>` +
              `<div class="t-row"><span>${YEARS[0]}</span><b>${pp(val(d.c, "p0", YEARS[0]))}</b></div>`, e);
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { bars.attr("opacity", 1); hideTip(); });
      });

      sect("ch1 so-what", () => {
        const spread = latestVals[latestVals.length - 1].v - latestVals[0].v;
        const inner = contrasts?.spread_median;
        document.getElementById("ch1-sowhat").innerHTML =
          `A single national figure of ${pp(national[national.length - 1].unweighted)} covers a ` +
          `${fmt1(spread)} pp range across ${latestVals.length} regencies. ` +
          (inner != null
            ? `And inside those regencies the model finds a further ${fmt1(inner)} pp of typical spread between kecamatan — variation no published statistic reaches.`
            : `Whatever variation exists <em>inside</em> a regency is invisible in the official series, which is the gap this case is built to fill.`);
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ CH2 — gates + skill ═════════════════════════════ */
      sect("gates", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("gate-grid");
        if (!statsJson) {
          const specs = [
            ["CHECK 1", "Out-of-sample skill", "R² ≥ 0.50 · Spearman ρ ≥ 0.70 · RMSE ≤ 4.0 pp", true],
            ["CHECK 2", "Java / off-Java disclosure", "both R² published; off-Java < 0.35 ⇒ labelled indicative", false],
            ["CHECK 3", "Temporal hold-out", "train ≤ 2023 → Spearman ρ ≥ 0.65 on 2024 and 2025", false],
            ["CHECK 4", "Benchmark integrity", "regency totals reproduced within 0.1 pp", true],
          ];
          const why = document.createElement("p");
          why.className = "sowhat pending-note";
          why.innerHTML =
            "<b>No numbers yet, on purpose.</b> The gates below carry their published " +
            "thresholds; their values arrive with the last data partition. Open Buildings " +
            "streams in geographic order, so a model fitted on a partial pull would be " +
            "<em>spatially biased</em>, not merely noisy — a half-loaded Indonesia is mostly " +
            "one half of Indonesia. Whatever the numbers turn out to be, they will be published " +
            "as measured: a failing gate goes up red.";
          el.parentElement.insertBefore(why, el);
          el.innerHTML = specs.map(([id, t, thr, hard]) => `
            <div class="gate pending">
              <div class="gate-top"><span class="gate-id">${id}</span>
                <span class="gate-status pending">PENDING</span></div>
              <h4>${t}${hard ? ' <span class="hard">hard</span>' : ""}</h4>
              <p class="cap">${thr}</p>
            </div>`).join("");
          return;
        }
        el.innerHTML = statsJson.gates.map((g, gi) => `
          <div class="gate ${g.status}">
            <div class="gate-top"><span class="gate-id">CHECK ${gi + 1}</span>
              <span class="gate-status ${g.status}">${g.status.toUpperCase()}</span></div>
            <h4>${g.title}${g.hard ? ' <span class="hard">hard</span>' : ""}</h4>
            <ul class="checks">${g.checks.map((c) => `
              <li class="${c.ok === null ? "unk" : c.ok ? "ok" : "bad"}">
                <span>${c.label}</span>
                <b>${c.value == null ? "—" : fmt2(c.value) + (c.unit ? " " + c.unit : "")}</b>
                <i>${c.cmp} ${c.threshold}${c.unit ? " " + c.unit : ""}</i>
              </li>`).join("")}</ul>
            <p class="cap">${g.detail}</p>
          </div>`).join("");
      });

      const scatterState = { cv: "lopo", reg: "all" };
      sect("scatter", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("scatter-chart");
        if (!ledger.scatter) {
          plate(el, "pending", "The validation scatter needs the fitted model.",
            PENDING_BODY);
          document.getElementById("cv-seg").classList.add("disabled");
          document.getElementById("reg-seg").classList.add("disabled");
          return;
        }
        const rows = ledger.scatter.rows.map(([code, y, lopo, rand, block, ridge, java, kota]) =>
          ({ code, y, lopo, random: rand, block, lopo_ridge: ridge, java, kota }));
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 470, M = { t: 16, r: 16, b: 44, l: 48 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img")
          .attr("aria-label", "Scatter of model predictions against official BPS regency rates");
        const lim = Math.max(d3.max(rows, (d) => d.y), d3.max(rows, (d) => d.lopo ?? 0)) * 1.06;
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, lim], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, lim], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(6).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSizeOuter(0)).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(6).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSize(-(W - M.l - M.r)))
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("line").attr("stroke", HAIR))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove()).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("text").attr("x", (M.l + W - M.r) / 2).attr("y", H - 6).attr("text-anchor", "middle")
          .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
          .text(`OFFICIAL BPS P0 · ${ledger.scatter.year}`);
        svg.append("text").attr("transform", `rotate(-90)`).attr("x", -(M.t + H - M.b) / 2).attr("y", 13)
          .attr("text-anchor", "middle").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED)
          .attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace").text("MODEL, HELD OUT");
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(0)).attr("y1", y(0)).attr("x2", x(lim)).attr("y2", y(lim))
          .attr("stroke", "#F0EAE1").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.28).attr("stroke-dasharray", "4 4");
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle.d").data(rows).join("circle").attr("class", "d")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.y)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.lopo ?? 0)).attr("r", 3.6)
          .attr("fill", OCHRE).attr("fill-opacity", 0.62)
          .attr("stroke", "#14100C").attr("stroke-width", 0.6);
        function redraw() {
          const active = (d) => scatterState.reg === "all" || (scatterState.reg === "java" ? d.java === 1 : d.java === 0);
          dots.transition().duration(DUR).ease(d3.easeCubicOut)
            .attr("cy", (d) => y(d[scatterState.cv] ?? 0))
            .attr("fill-opacity", (d) => (active(d) ? 0.68 : 0.06))
            .attr("r", (d) => (active(d) ? 3.6 : 2.2));
        }
        dots.on("mousemove", (e, d) => {
          const p = d[scatterState.cv];
          showTip(`<b>${nameOf(d.code)}</b><span class="t-sub">${provOf(d.code)} · ${d.kota ? "kota" : "kabupaten"} · ${d.java ? "Java" : "off-Java"}</span>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Official BPS ${ledger.scatter.year}</span><b class="teal">${pp(d.y)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Model, held out</span><b class="ochre">${pp(p)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Error</span><b>${p == null ? "—" : `${p - d.y > 0 ? "+" : ""}${fmt1(p - d.y)} pp`}</b></div>`, e);
        }).on("mouseleave", hideTip);
        document.querySelectorAll("#cv-seg button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
          document.querySelectorAll("#cv-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
          scatterState.cv = b.dataset.cv; redraw();
        }));
        document.querySelectorAll("#reg-seg button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
          document.querySelectorAll("#reg-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
          scatterState.reg = b.dataset.reg; redraw();
        }));
      });

      sect("scheme chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("scheme-chart");
        if (!statsJson) { plate(el, "pending", "Fold comparison pending.", PENDING_BODY); return; }
        const s = statsJson.skill;
        const rows = [
          { k: "Random k-fold", v: s.random?.r2, note: "leaks neighbours — shown for contrast only", bad: true },
          { k: "200 km blocks", v: s.block?.r2, note: "spatial sensitivity" },
          { k: "Leave-one-province-out", v: s.lopo?.r2, note: "the headline number", head: true },
          { k: "Ridge baseline (LOPO)", v: s.lopo_ridge?.r2, note: "linear, same folds" },
        ].filter((r) => r.v != null);
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 176, M = { t: 8, r: 60, b: 22, l: 176 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img").attr("aria-label", "R squared by cross-validation scheme");
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, Math.max(0.9, d3.max(rows, (r) => r.v))], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const yb = d3.scaleBand(rows.map((r) => r.k), [M.t, H - M.b]).padding(0.28);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(yb).tickSize(0))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove())
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("text").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", (d) => (d.startsWith("Leave") ? "#F0EAE1" : MUTED))
            .attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace"));
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(0.5)).attr("x2", x(0.5)).attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b)
          .attr("stroke", OCHRE).attr("stroke-opacity", 0.5).attr("stroke-dasharray", "3 3");
        svg.append("text").attr("x", x(0.5)).attr("y", H - 7).attr("text-anchor", "middle")
          .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", OCHRE).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
          .text("gate 0.50");
        const g = svg.selectAll("g.r").data(rows).join("g").attr("class", "r");
        g.append("rect").attr("x", x(0)).attr("y", (d) => yb(d.k)).attr("height", yb.bandwidth())
          .attr("rx", 2).attr("fill", (d) => (d.head ? OCHRE : d.bad ? "#6B7CA6" : "#8A5A22"))
          .attr("width", 0).transition().duration(DUR).ease(d3.easeCubicOut)
          .attr("width", (d) => Math.max(1, x(d.v) - x(0)));
        g.append("text").attr("x", (d) => x(d.v) + 8).attr("y", (d) => yb(d.k) + yb.bandwidth() / 2 + 4)
          .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", "#F0EAE1").attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
          .text((d) => fmt2(d.v));
        g.on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(`<b>${d.k}</b><div class="t-row"><span>R²</span><b>${fmt2(d.v)}</b></div>` +
          `<span class="t-sub">${d.note}</span>`, e)).on("mouseleave", hideTip);
      });

      sect("temporal chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("temporal-chart");
        if (!ledger.scatter?.temporal?.length || !statsJson) {
          plate(el, "pending", "Temporal hold-out pending.", PENDING_BODY); return;
        }
        // plotted against the STRICT hold-out (province held out as well as the year); the
        // same-province variant is in the tooltip, because on its own it mostly measures
        // how little a regency's rate moves from one release to the next.
        const rows = ledger.scatter.temporal
          .map(([yr, obs, loose, strict, code]) => ({ yr, obs, pred: strict ?? loose, loose, strict, code }))
          .filter((d) => d.pred != null);
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 176, M = { t: 12, r: 12, b: 30, l: 42 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img")
          .attr("aria-label", "Temporal hold-out: predictions for 2024 and 2025 against the official rates");
        const lim = d3.max(rows, (d) => Math.max(d.obs, d.pred)) * 1.05;
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, lim], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, lim], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(5).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSizeOuter(0)).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(4).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSize(-(W - M.l - M.r)))
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("line").attr("stroke", HAIR))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove()).call(axisStyle);
        svg.append("line").attr("x1", x(0)).attr("y1", y(0)).attr("x2", x(lim)).attr("y2", y(lim))
          .attr("stroke", "#F0EAE1").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.25).attr("stroke-dasharray", "4 4");
        const cols = { 2024: "#8A5A22", 2025: OCHRE };
        svg.selectAll("circle").data(rows).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.obs)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.pred)).attr("r", 2.6)
          .attr("fill", (d) => cols[d.yr] ?? OCHRE).attr("fill-opacity", 0.55)
          .on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(`<b>${nameOf(d.code)} · ${d.yr} release</b>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Official</span><b class="teal">${pp(d.obs)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Year <i>and</i> province unseen</span><b class="ochre">${pp(d.strict)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Year unseen only</span><b>${pp(d.loose)}</b></div>`, e))
          .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
        const leg = svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l + 6},${M.t + 4})`);
        Object.entries(cols).forEach(([yr, c], i) => {
          const st = statsJson.skill[`temporal_strict_${yr}`]?.spearman;
          const lo = statsJson.skill[`temporal_${yr}`]?.spearman;
          const gg = leg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${i * 16})`);
          gg.append("circle").attr("r", 3.4).attr("fill", c);
          gg.append("text").attr("x", 10).attr("y", 4).attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED)
            .attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
            .text(`${yr} · ρ ${st != null ? fmt2(st) : "—"} strict · ${lo != null ? fmt2(lo) : "—"} same-province`);
        });
      });

      sect("ch2 so-what", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("ch2-sowhat");
        if (!statsJson) {
          el.innerHTML = "The gates above carry their thresholds now and their numbers as soon " +
            "as the last data partition lands. A failing gate will be published red, with its " +
            "value — the lab does not tune the data to the story.";
          return;
        }
        const s = statsJson.skill;
        const g1 = statsJson.gates[0];
        const dec = statsJson.decomposition || {};
        const inflate = s.random?.r2 != null && s.lopo?.r2 != null ? s.random.r2 - s.lopo.r2 : null;
        el.innerHTML =
          (g1.status === "pass"
            ? `The model reproduces the official ranking of ${s.lopo.n} regencies it was never trained on (Spearman ρ ${fmt2(s.lopo.spearman)}, RMSE ${fmt1(s.lopo.rmse)} pp). `
            : `<b class="bad-inline">The held-out skill check fails on this run and goes up red</b> — R² ${fmt2(s.lopo.r2)}, ρ ${fmt2(s.lopo.spearman)}, RMSE ${fmt1(s.lopo.rmse)} pp against thresholds of 0.50, 0.70 and 4.0 pp. Those thresholds came from studies that correlated an index with official rates on the units they already covered — none of them held space out, and this number does. `) +
          (inflate != null
            ? `A random k-fold on the same rows would have reported R² ${fmt2(s.random.r2)} instead of ${fmt2(s.lopo.r2)} — ${fmt2(inflate)} of pure fold design, and the reason the honest number is the published one. `
            : "") +
          (dec.offset_share_of_sse != null
            ? `<b>${d3.format(".0%")(dec.offset_share_of_sse)} of the squared error is a single constant offset for a whole province</b> — the model pulls every regency toward the middle, so it under-calls the poorest provinces and over-calls the least poor. Strip the offsets and regencies are ordered inside their province at ρ ${fmt2(dec.within_province_spearman)} across ${dec.provinces_scored} provinces, though only R² ${fmt2(dec.within_province_r2)} of the within-province variation: the weaker half of the job, but the half chapter 4 actually needs, because benchmarking takes the level from BPS. `
            : "") +
          (s.temporal_strict_2025?.spearman != null
            ? `The temporal test tells the same story twice: ρ ${fmt2(s.temporal_2025.spearman)} when the model has seen the regency in earlier years, ρ ${fmt2(s.temporal_strict_2025.spearman)} when the province is held out too. `
            : "") +
          `Off-Java R² is ${s.lopo_offjava?.r2 == null ? "—" : fmt2(s.lopo_offjava.r2)} against ${s.lopo_java?.r2 == null ? "—" : fmt2(s.lopo_java.r2)} on Java — but R² is scaled by each group's own spread, and in percentage points the off-Java error is ${s.lopo_offjava?.rmse == null ? "—" : fmt1(s.lopo_offjava.rmse)} pp against Java's ${s.lopo_java?.rmse == null ? "—" : fmt1(s.lopo_java.rmse)} pp, so read both. Urban kota R² is ${s.lopo_kota?.r2 == null ? "—" : fmt2(s.lopo_kota.r2)}` +
          (statsJson.kota_indicative || statsJson.offjava_indicative
            ? " — below zero for cities, so every kota estimate here is labelled indicative."
            : ".");
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ CH3 — signals ═══════════════════════════════════ */
      sect("family chart", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("family-chart");
        if (!ledger.families) { plate(el, "pending", "Feature attribution pending.", PENDING_BODY); return; }
        document.getElementById("shap-unit").textContent = ledger.families.unit;
        const rows = ledger.families.rows.map(([k, v, share]) => ({ k, v, share }));
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 250, M = { t: 8, r: 66, b: 20, l: 150 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img").attr("aria-label", "Feature families ranked by contribution");
        const x = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(rows, (r) => r.v) * 1.02], [M.l, W - M.r]);
        const yb = d3.scaleBand(rows.map((r) => r.k), [M.t, H - M.b]).padding(0.3);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(yb).tickSize(0))
          .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove())
          .call((g) => g.selectAll("text").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", "#F0EAE1"));
        const defs = svg.append("defs");
        const lg = defs.append("linearGradient").attr("id", "famg").attr("x1", 0).attr("x2", 1);
        lg.append("stop").attr("offset", "0%").attr("stop-color", "#7A4F1E");
        lg.append("stop").attr("offset", "100%").attr("stop-color", OCHRE);
        const g = svg.selectAll("g.f").data(rows).join("g").attr("class", "f");
        g.append("rect").attr("x", x(0)).attr("y", (d) => yb(d.k)).attr("height", yb.bandwidth())
          .attr("rx", 2).attr("fill", "url(#famg)").attr("width", 0)
          .transition().duration(DUR).ease(d3.easeCubicOut).delay((d, i) => (reduced ? 0 : i * 60))
          .attr("width", (d) => Math.max(1, x(d.v) - x(0)));
        g.append("text").attr("x", (d) => x(d.v) + 8).attr("y", (d) => yb(d.k) + yb.bandwidth() / 2 + 4)
          .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
          .text((d) => d3.format(".0%")(d.share));
        g.on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(`<b>${d.k}</b>` +
          `<div class="t-row"><span>${ledger.families.unit}</span><b>${fmt2(d.v)}</b></div>` +
          `<div class="t-row"><span>Share of all attribution</span><b>${d3.format(".1%")(d.share)}</b></div>`, e))
          .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
      });

      sect("drilldown", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("drill-chart");
        const read = document.getElementById("drill-read");
        const pick = document.getElementById("shap-pick");
        const withShap = codes.filter((c) => REG[c]?.shap?.length);
        if (!withShap.length) {
          plate(el, "pending", "Per-regency attribution pending.", PENDING_BODY);
          pick.disabled = true;
          pick.innerHTML = "<option>—</option>";
          return;
        }
        withShap.sort((a, b) => d3.ascending(nameOf(a), nameOf(b)));
        pick.innerHTML = withShap.map((c) => `<option value="${c}">${nameOf(c)} · ${provOf(c)}</option>`).join("");
        const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), H = 250, M = { t: 8, r: 16, b: 24, l: 8 };
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H)
          .attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`).attr("role", "img").attr("aria-label", "Top five signals for the selected regency");
        const gAx = svg.append("g"), gBar = svg.append("g");
        function draw(code) {
          const rows = (REG[code].shap || []).map(([f, v, phrase]) => ({ f, v, phrase }));
          const lim = d3.max(rows, (r) => Math.abs(r.v)) * 1.25 || 1;
          const x = d3.scaleLinear([-lim, lim], [M.l + 4, W - M.r]);
          const yb = d3.scaleBand(rows.map((r) => r.phrase), [M.t, H - M.b]).padding(0.34);
          gAx.selectAll("*").remove();
          gAx.append("line").attr("x1", x(0)).attr("x2", x(0)).attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b)
            .attr("stroke", HAIR);
          gAx.append("text").attr("x", x(0) - 6).attr("y", H - 8).attr("text-anchor", "end")
            .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
            .text("← lowers the estimate");
          gAx.append("text").attr("x", x(0) + 6).attr("y", H - 8)
            .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
            .text("raises it →");
          const sel = gBar.selectAll("g.s").data(rows, (d) => d.f);
          sel.exit().remove();
          const ent = sel.enter().append("g").attr("class", "s");
          ent.append("rect").attr("rx", 2);
          ent.append("text").attr("class", "lab");
          const all = ent.merge(sel);
          all.select("rect")
            .attr("y", (d) => yb(d.phrase)).attr("height", yb.bandwidth())
            .attr("fill", (d) => (d.v >= 0 ? OCHRE : "#6B7CA6"))
            .transition().duration(DUR).ease(d3.easeCubicOut)
            .attr("x", (d) => (d.v >= 0 ? x(0) : x(d.v)))
            .attr("width", (d) => Math.max(1.5, Math.abs(x(d.v) - x(0))));
          // label on the empty side of the axis, never on top of its own bar
          all.select("text.lab")
            .attr("y", (d) => yb(d.phrase) + yb.bandwidth() / 2 + 4)
            .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", "#F0EAE1")
            .attr("text-anchor", (d) => (d.v >= 0 ? "end" : "start"))
            .attr("x", (d) => (d.v >= 0 ? x(0) - 10 : x(0) + 10))
            .text((d) => `${d.phrase} (${d.v > 0 ? "+" : ""}${fmt2(d.v)} pp)`);
          all.on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(`<b>${d.phrase}</b><span class="t-sub">${d.f}</span>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Contribution</span><b class="${d.v >= 0 ? "ochre" : ""}">${d.v > 0 ? "+" : ""}${fmt2(d.v)} pp</b></div>`, e))
            .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
          const up = rows.filter((r) => r.v > 0).slice(0, 2).map((r) => r.phrase);
          const dn = rows.filter((r) => r.v < 0).slice(0, 2).map((r) => r.phrase);
          const off = val(code, "p0", LATEST), pr = REG[code].pred;
          read.innerHTML =
            `<b>${nameOf(code)}</b> — official <b class="teal">${pp(off)}</b>, held-out prediction ` +
            `<b class="ochre">${pp(pr)}</b>. ` +
            (up.length ? `The model reads ${up.join(" and ")} and pushes the estimate up. ` : "") +
            (dn.length ? `${up.length ? "Against that, " : "The model reads "}${dn.join(" and ")}, pulling it down.` : "");
        }
        pick.addEventListener("change", () => draw(pick.value));
        draw(withShap[0]);
      });

      sect("ch3 so-what", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("ch3-sowhat");
        if (!ledger.families) {
          el.innerHTML = "The attribution chart names the signal families and, once fitted, " +
            "ranks them — so a client can argue with the model rather than accept it.";
          return;
        }
        const top = ledger.families.rows[0];
        el.innerHTML = `${top[0]} alone accounts for ${d3.format(".0%")(top[2])} of the model's ` +
          `attribution. Read that as what the model <em>uses</em>, not as what it earns: ` +
          `attribution is measured in-sample, and held out province by province the roof family ` +
          `improves the <em>ordering</em> of regencies far more than the level of their rates. ` +
          `It is also a warning about time — the roof and land-cover layers are single-vintage, ` +
          `so this model reads <em>where</em> poverty is far better than <em>when</em> it changes.`;
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ CH4 — below the line ════════════════════════════ */
      sect("intervals", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("interval-chart");
        const pick = document.getElementById("reg-pick");
        if (!estimates) {
          plate(el, "pending", "Kecamatan estimates pending.", PENDING_BODY);
          pick.disabled = true; pick.innerHTML = "<option>—</option>";
          return;
        }
        const byParent = new Map();
        estimates.pcodes.forEach((p, i) => {
          const par = estimates.parents[i];
          if (!par) return;
          if (!byParent.has(par)) byParent.set(par, []);
          byParent.get(par).push(i);
        });
        const parents = [...byParent.keys()].filter((c) => byParent.get(c).length > 1)
          .sort((a, b) => d3.ascending(nameOf(a), nameOf(b)));
        pick.innerHTML = parents.map((c) => `<option value="${c}">${nameOf(c)} · ${provOf(c)}</option>`).join("");
        const svgSel = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("role", "img");
        function draw(code) {
          const idxs = byParent.get(code) || [];
          const yearKey = String(estimates.latest);
          const rows = idxs.map((i) => ({
            name: estimates.names[i], est: estimates.est[yearKey][i],
            lo: estimates.lo[i], hi: estimates.hi[i], pop: estimates.pop[i],
          })).filter((r) => r.est != null).sort((a, b) => d3.descending(a.est, b.est));
          const rowH = 20, H = Math.max(160, rows.length * rowH + 62);
          const W = Math.max(el.clientWidth, 280), M = { t: 26, r: 54, b: 30, l: 132 };
          svgSel.attr("height", H).attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`)
            .attr("aria-label", `Kecamatan poverty estimates inside ${nameOf(code)} with intervals`);
          svgSel.selectAll("*").remove();
          const official = val(code, "p0", estimates.latest);
          const lim = [0, Math.max(d3.max(rows, (r) => r.hi ?? r.est) ?? 10, official ?? 0) * 1.08];
          const x = d3.scaleLinear(lim, [M.l, W - M.r]);
          const yb = d3.scaleBand(rows.map((r) => r.name), [M.t, H - M.b]).padding(0.32);
          svgSel.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
            .call(d3.axisBottom(x).ticks(5).tickFormat((v) => `${v}%`).tickSizeOuter(0)).call(axisStyle);
          svgSel.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`).call(d3.axisLeft(yb).tickSize(0))
            .call((g) => g.select(".domain").remove())
            .call((g) => g.selectAll("text").attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED));
          if (official != null) {
            svgSel.append("rect").attr("x", x(official) - 1).attr("y", M.t)
              .attr("width", 2).attr("height", H - M.b - M.t).attr("fill", TEAL).attr("opacity", 0.9);
            svgSel.append("text").attr("x", x(official)).attr("y", M.t - 10)
              .attr("text-anchor", x(official) > W - M.r - 90 ? "end" : "middle")
              .attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", TEAL).attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace")
              .text(`OFFICIAL BPS ${fmt1(official)}%`);
          }
          const g = svgSel.selectAll("g.k").data(rows).join("g").attr("class", "k");
          g.append("line").attr("y1", (d) => yb(d.name) + yb.bandwidth() / 2)
            .attr("y2", (d) => yb(d.name) + yb.bandwidth() / 2)
            .attr("stroke", "#8A5A22").attr("stroke-width", 3).attr("stroke-linecap", "round")
            .attr("x1", (d) => x(d.est)).attr("x2", (d) => x(d.est))
            .transition().duration(DUR).ease(d3.easeCubicOut)
            .attr("x1", (d) => x(d.lo ?? d.est)).attr("x2", (d) => x(d.hi ?? d.est));
          g.append("circle").attr("cy", (d) => yb(d.name) + yb.bandwidth() / 2)
            .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.est)).attr("r", 4).attr("fill", OCHRE)
            .attr("stroke", "#14100C").attr("stroke-width", 1);
          g.on("mousemove", (e, d) => showTip(`<b>${d.name}</b><span class="t-sub">kecamatan of ${nameOf(code)}</span>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Model estimate ${estimates.latest}</span><b class="ochre">${pp(d.est)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Interval</span><b>${pp(d.lo)} – ${pp(d.hi)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Official regency rate</span><b class="teal">${pp(official)}</b></div>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Population</span><b>${d.pop == null ? "—" : fmtI(d.pop)}</b></div>`, e))
            .on("mouseleave", hideTip);
        }
        pick.addEventListener("change", () => draw(pick.value));
        draw(parents[0]);
        addEventListener("resize", () => draw(pick.value));
      });

      sect("contrasts", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("contrast-list");
        if (!contrasts) { plate(el, "pending", "Confident contrasts pending.", PENDING_BODY); return; }
        el.innerHTML = `<ol class="contrasts">` + contrasts.pairs.map((p) => `
          <li>
            <div class="cpair">
              <span class="cname">${p.high.name}</span>
              <span class="cval ochre">${fmt1(p.high.est)}%</span>
              <span class="cbar"><i style="width:${Math.min(100, (p.high.est / (contrasts.pairs[0].high.est || 1)) * 100)}%"></i></span>
            </div>
            <div class="cpair low">
              <span class="cname">${p.low.name}</span>
              <span class="cval">${fmt1(p.low.est)}%</span>
              <span class="cbar"><i style="width:${Math.min(100, (p.low.est / (contrasts.pairs[0].high.est || 1)) * 100)}%"></i></span>
            </div>
            <span class="cmeta stamp">${nameOf(p.code)} · ${p.prov} · OFFICIAL ${fmt1(p.official)}% · GAP ${fmt1(p.gap)} pp · INTERVALS ${fmt1(p.high.lo)}–${fmt1(p.high.hi)} vs ${fmt1(p.low.lo)}–${fmt1(p.low.hi)}</span>
          </li>`).join("") + "</ol>";
      });

      sect("ch4 so-what", () => {
        const el = document.getElementById("ch4-sowhat");
        if (!contrasts || !estimates) {
          el.innerHTML = "Once the estimates land, this chapter reports how many kecamatan pairs " +
            "inside a single regency are separable at the published interval — the honest measure " +
            "of how much resolution the model really adds.";
          return;
        }
        const dis = statsJson?.disaggregation;
        el.innerHTML =
          `Inside a typical regency the model spreads the official rate over ` +
          `${fmt1(contrasts.spread_median)} pp of range, reaching ${fmt1(contrasts.spread_max)} pp ` +
          `at the extreme — variation the published series cannot show. But only ` +
          `<b>${fmtI(contrasts.n_separable)} of ${fmtI(contrasts.n_regencies)}</b> regencies have a ` +
          `poorest and a least-poor kecamatan whose intervals actually clear each other, because ` +
          `those intervals carry the province's own out-of-sample error. ` +
          (dis?.benchmarked_model
            ? `Nothing official exists below the regency, so this layer cannot be scored where it ` +
              `operates — but the identical rule can be scored one level up. Given each province's ` +
              `official rate and asked to distribute it among that province's regencies, the ` +
              `held-out model beats giving every regency its province's rate on ` +
              `<b>${d3.format(".1%")(dis.win_rate)} of ${fmtI(dis.n)}</b> regencies, cutting mean ` +
              `error from ${fmt2(dis.flat_parent_rate.mae)} pp to ` +
              `<b>${fmt2(dis.benchmarked_model.mae)} pp</b> and lifting R² from ` +
              `${fmt2(dis.flat_parent_rate.r2)} to ${fmt2(dis.benchmarked_model.r2)}. That is the ` +
              `honest measure of what disaggregation adds, and it is a real margin rather than a ` +
              `large one. `
            : "") +
          `A map fine enough to argue about, honest enough to say where the argument stops.`;
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ EXPLORE ═════════════════════════════════════════ */
      sect("explore", () => {
        const state = { level: "adm2", metric: "p0", year: LATEST, code: null };
        const mapEl = document.getElementById("map");
        const legendEl = document.getElementById("legend");
        const panel = document.getElementById("panel");
        let cmap = null, useMaplibre = false, ml = null, currentLayer = ADM2;

        const METRIC = {
          p0: { label: "Poverty headcount P0", unit: "%", fmt: (v) => pp(v), ramp: offScale },
          p1: { label: "Poverty gap P1", unit: "index", fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : fmt2(v)), ramp: offScale },
          p2: { label: "Poverty severity P2", unit: "index", fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : fmt2(v)), ramp: offScale },
          line: { label: "Poverty line", unit: "Rp/person/month",
                  fmt: (v) => (v == null ? "—" : `Rp ${fmtI(v)}`), ramp: offScale },
        };

        function valuesFor() {
          const m = new Map();
          if (state.level === "adm2") {
            for (const u of currentLayer.units) m.set(u.id, val(u.id, state.metric, state.year));
          } else if (estimates) {
            const key = String(state.year);
            const arr = estimates.est[key];
            const idx = new Map(estimates.pcodes.map((p, i) => [p, i]));
            for (const u of currentLayer.units) {
              const i = idx.get(u.id);
              m.set(u.id, arr && i != null ? arr[i] : null);
            }
          }
          return m;
        }
        function scaleFor(vals) {
          const finite = [...vals.values()].filter((v) => v != null && isFinite(v)).sort(d3.ascending);
          const lo = finite.length ? finite[0] : 0;
          const hi = finite.length ? (d3.quantile(finite, 0.98) ?? finite[finite.length - 1]) : 1;
          const ramp = state.level === "adm3" ? povScale : METRIC[state.metric].ramp;
          return { lo, hi, colour: (v) => (v == null || !isFinite(v) ? "#1A1610" : ramp(Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (v - lo) / (hi - lo || 1))))) };
        }
        function legend(sc) {
          const stops = d3.range(0, 1.001, 0.05).map((t) => sc.colour(sc.lo + t * (sc.hi - sc.lo)));
          legendEl.innerHTML =
            `<span class="lg-title stamp">${state.level === "adm2" ? "OFFICIAL BPS" : "MODEL ESTIMATE"} · ${METRIC[state.metric].label.toUpperCase()} · ${state.year}</span>` +
            `<span class="lg-ramp" style="background:linear-gradient(90deg,${stops.join(",")})"></span>` +
            `<span class="lg-ends stamp"><b>${METRIC[state.metric].fmt(sc.lo)}</b><b>${METRIC[state.metric].fmt(sc.hi)}</b></span>` +
            (state.level === "adm3"
              ? `<span class="lg-note stamp">MODEL ESTIMATE · BENCHMARKED TO THE OFFICIAL REGENCY RATE${statsJson?.offjava_indicative ? " · OFF-JAVA INDICATIVE" : ""}${statsJson?.kota_indicative ? " · KOTA INDICATIVE" : ""}</span>`
              : `<span class="lg-note stamp">SOURCE: BPS MARCH SUSENAS · ${currentLayer.units.length} UNITS</span>`);
        }
        const tipFor = (u) => {
          if (state.level === "adm2") {
            const parts = ["p0", "p1", "p2", "line"].map((k) =>
              `<div class="t-row"><span>${METRIC[k].label}</span><b class="${k === state.metric ? "teal" : ""}">${METRIC[k].fmt(val(u.id, k, state.year))}</b></div>`).join("");
            return `<b>${u.name}</b><span class="t-sub">${provOf(u.id)} · BPS ${state.year} · official</span>${parts}`;
          }
          const key = String(state.year);
          const i = estIdx?.get(u.id) ?? -1;
          const est = i >= 0 ? estimates.est[key]?.[i] : null;
          const off = val(u.parent, "p0", state.year);
          return `<b>${u.name}</b><span class="t-sub">kecamatan of ${nameOf(u.parent)} · ${provOf(u.parent)}</span>` +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Model estimate ${state.year}</span><b class="ochre">${pp(est)}</b></div>` +
            (i >= 0 && estimates.lo[i] != null && state.year === estimates.latest
              ? `<div class="t-row"><span>Interval</span><b>${pp(estimates.lo[i])} – ${pp(estimates.hi[i])}</b></div>` : "") +
            `<div class="t-row"><span>Official regency rate</span><b class="teal">${pp(off)}</b></div>`;
        };

        function openPanel(u) {
          panel.hidden = false;
          const isReg = state.level === "adm2";
          const code = isReg ? u.id : u.parent;
          state.code = u.id;
          cmap?.setSelected(u.id);
          document.getElementById("panel-kind").textContent = isReg ? "REGENCY · OFFICIAL" : "KECAMATAN · MODEL ESTIMATE";
          document.getElementById("panel-name").textContent = u.name;
          document.getElementById("panel-sub").textContent =
            isReg ? `${provOf(code)} · BPS CODE ${code}` : `${nameOf(code)} · ${provOf(code)}`;
          const nums = document.getElementById("panel-nums");
          if (isReg) {
            nums.innerHTML = ["p0", "p1", "p2", "line"].map((k) =>
              `<div class="pn"><span>${METRIC[k].label}</span><b class="teal">${METRIC[k].fmt(val(code, k, state.year))}</b></div>`).join("") +
              (REG[code]?.pred != null ? `<div class="pn"><span>Model, held out</span><b class="ochre">${pp(REG[code].pred)}</b></div>` : "") +
              (REG[code]?.pop != null ? `<div class="pn"><span>Population ${LATEST}</span><b>${fmtI(REG[code].pop)}</b></div>` : "") +
              (REG[code]?.adm3 ? `<div class="pn"><span>Kecamatan</span><b>${REG[code].adm3}</b></div>` : "");
          } else {
            const i = estIdx?.get(u.id) ?? -1;
            const est = i >= 0 ? estimates.est[String(state.year)]?.[i] : null;
            nums.innerHTML =
              `<div class="pn"><span>Model estimate ${state.year}</span><b class="ochre">${pp(est)}</b></div>` +
              (i >= 0 && state.year === estimates.latest
                ? `<div class="pn"><span>Interval</span><b>${pp(estimates.lo[i])} – ${pp(estimates.hi[i])}</b></div>` +
                  `<div class="pn"><span>Population</span><b>${estimates.pop[i] == null ? "—" : fmtI(estimates.pop[i])}</b></div>` +
                  `<div class="pn"><span>Benchmark factor</span><b>${estimates.factor[i] == null ? "—" : fmt2(estimates.factor[i])}×</b></div>` : "") +
              `<div class="pn"><span>Official regency rate</span><b class="teal">${pp(val(code, "p0", state.year))}</b></div>`;
          }
          // sparkline of the official regency series, always shown for context
          const spark = d3.select("#panel-spark").html("");
          const series = YEARS.map((y) => ({ y, v: val(code, "p0", y) })).filter((d) => d.v != null);
          if (series.length > 1) {
            const W = 250, H = 62;
            const x = d3.scaleLinear(d3.extent(series, (d) => d.y), [6, W - 6]);
            const y = d3.scaleLinear([d3.min(series, (d) => d.v) * 0.9, d3.max(series, (d) => d.v) * 1.05], [H - 12, 8]);
            const svg = spark.append("svg").attr("width", "100%").attr("height", H).attr("viewBox", `0 0 ${W} ${H}`);
            svg.append("path").datum(series).attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", TEAL).attr("stroke-width", 1.8)
              .attr("d", d3.line().x((d) => x(d.y)).y((d) => y(d.v)).curve(d3.curveMonotoneX));
            svg.selectAll("circle").data(series).join("circle").attr("cx", (d) => x(d.y)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.v))
              .attr("r", (d) => (d.y === state.year ? 3.6 : 1.8)).attr("fill", (d) => (d.y === state.year ? "#F0EAE1" : TEAL));
            svg.append("text").attr("x", 6).attr("y", H - 1).attr("font-size", 12).attr("fill", MUTED)
              .attr("font-family", "IBM Plex Mono, monospace").text(`OFFICIAL P0 ${YEARS[0]}–${LATEST}`);
          }
          const sh = document.getElementById("panel-shap");
          const rows = REG[code]?.shap;
          // attribution is fitted at the regency level, so say whose it is when the panel
          // is showing a kecamatan
          sh.innerHTML = rows?.length
            ? `<span class="stamp dim">WHY THE MODEL SAYS SO${isReg ? "" : ` — FOR ${String(nameOf(code)).toUpperCase()}, THE REGENCY`}</span><ul class="mini-shap">` +
              rows.map(([f, v, phrase]) => `<li class="${v >= 0 ? "up" : "down"}"><span>${phrase}</span><b>${v > 0 ? "+" : ""}${fmt2(v)} pp</b></li>`).join("") + "</ul>"
            : "";
          syncHash();
        }
        document.getElementById("panel-close").addEventListener("click", () => {
          panel.hidden = true; state.code = null; cmap?.setSelected(null); syncHash();
        });

        function syncHash() {
          const p = new URLSearchParams();
          p.set("l", state.level); p.set("m", state.metric); p.set("y", String(state.year));
          if (state.code) p.set("c", state.code);
          history.replaceState(null, "", `#${p.toString()}`);
        }

        function repaint() {
          const vals = valuesFor();
          const sc = scaleFor(vals);
          legend(sc);
          if (cmap) cmap.setColours(currentLayer.units.map((u) => sc.colour(vals.get(u.id))));
          if (ml && useMaplibre) {
            for (const f of ml.geo.features) f.properties.col = sc.colour(vals.get(f.properties.id));
            ml.map.getSource("units")?.setData(ml.geo);
          }
          renderTable(vals);
        }

        function mountCanvas() {
          cmap = CanvasMap(mapEl, { ground: "#100D0A", pannable: true, tip: tipFor, onPick: openPanel });
          cmap.setLayer(currentLayer);
          const tag = document.createElement("span");
          tag.className = "map-tag stamp";
          tag.textContent = "2-D MAP · NO GPU REQUIRED · DRAG TO PAN · SCROLL TO ZOOM · COD-AB CC BY-IGO";
          mapEl.appendChild(tag);
        }

        // try MapLibre; on any failure (this browser runs with WebGL off) use the 2-D canvas,
        // which is a full-function renderer, not a placeholder.
        (async () => {
          try {
            const maplibregl = (await import("maplibre-gl")).default;
            if (!maplibregl.supported?.({ failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat: false })) throw new Error("WebGL unavailable");
            const geo = toGeoJSON(currentLayer);
            const map = new maplibregl.Map({
              container: mapEl, attributionControl: false, dragRotate: false,
              style: { version: 8, sources: {}, layers: [{ id: "bg", type: "background", paint: { "background-color": "#100D0A" } }] },
              bounds: [[currentLayer.bbox[0], currentLayer.bbox[1]], [currentLayer.bbox[2], currentLayer.bbox[3]]],
              fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 16 },
            });
            map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }));
            map.addControl(new maplibregl.AttributionControl({ compact: true, customAttribution: "BPS · HDX COD-AB CC BY-IGO" }));
            await new Promise((ok, no) => { map.on("load", ok); map.on("error", (e) => no(e.error ?? new Error("map error"))); });
            map.addSource("units", { type: "geojson", data: geo, promoteId: "id" });
            map.addLayer({ id: "fill", type: "fill", source: "units", paint: { "fill-color": ["get", "col"], "fill-opacity": 0.94 } });
            map.addLayer({ id: "line", type: "line", source: "units", paint: { "line-color": HAIR, "line-width": 0.4 } });
            ml = { map, geo }; useMaplibre = true;
            map.on("mousemove", "fill", (e) => showTip(tipFor(currentLayer.units[currentLayer.index.get(e.features[0].properties.id)]), e.originalEvent));
            map.on("mouseleave", "fill", hideTip);
            map.on("click", "fill", (e) => openPanel(currentLayer.units[currentLayer.index.get(e.features[0].properties.id)]));
            repaint();
          } catch (err) {
            console.warn("WebGL map unavailable — 2-D canvas renderer:", err?.message ?? err);
            useMaplibre = false; ml = null;
            mountCanvas();
            repaint();
          }
        })();

        /* ---- controls ---- */
        const yearRange = document.getElementById("year-range");
        yearRange.max = String(YEARS.length - 1);
        yearRange.value = String(YEARS.length - 1);
        const yearOut = document.getElementById("year-out");
        yearRange.addEventListener("input", () => {
          state.year = YEARS[+yearRange.value];
          yearOut.textContent = String(state.year);
          repaint();
          if (state.code) { const i = currentLayer.index.get(state.code); if (i != null) openPanel(currentLayer.units[i]); }
        });

        document.querySelectorAll("#metric-seg button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
          if (state.level === "adm3") return;
          document.querySelectorAll("#metric-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
          state.metric = b.dataset.metric; repaint(); syncHash();
        }));

        async function setLevel(lvl) {
          if (lvl === "adm3") {
            if (!estimates) { failBanner("Kecamatan estimates are not built yet — the regency view stays selected."); return; }
            await loadAdm3();
            if (!ADM3) { failBanner("Kecamatan geometry unavailable."); return; }
            currentLayer = ADM3; state.metric = "p0";
            document.querySelectorAll("#metric-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x.dataset.metric === "p0"));
            document.getElementById("metric-seg").classList.add("disabled");
          } else {
            currentLayer = ADM2;
            document.getElementById("metric-seg").classList.remove("disabled");
          }
          state.level = lvl; state.code = null; panel.hidden = true;
          if (useMaplibre && ml) { ml.geo = toGeoJSON(currentLayer); ml.map.getSource("units").setData(ml.geo); }
          else if (cmap) cmap.setLayer(currentLayer);
          repaint(); syncHash();
        }
        document.querySelectorAll("#lvl-seg button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
          document.querySelectorAll("#lvl-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
          setLevel(b.dataset.lvl);
        }));
        if (!estimates) {
          const b = document.querySelector('#lvl-seg [data-lvl="adm3"]');
          b.disabled = true;
          b.title = "Kecamatan estimates are produced by the model run, which is still pending";
          b.textContent = "Kecamatan · pending";
        }

        /* ---- table view + CSV ---- */
        const tableWrap = document.getElementById("table-wrap");
        const table = document.getElementById("data-table");
        let tableStale = true;
        function buildRows(vals) {
          const rows = currentLayer.units.map((u) => {
            const v = vals.get(u.id);
            return state.level === "adm2"
              ? { code: u.id, name: u.name, province: provOf(u.id), value: v,
                  official_p0: val(u.id, "p0", state.year), model_p0: REG[u.id]?.pred ?? null }
              : { code: u.id, name: u.name, regency: nameOf(u.parent), province: provOf(u.parent),
                  estimate_p0: v, official_regency_p0: val(u.parent, "p0", state.year) };
          }).filter((r) => Object.values(r).some((x) => x != null));
          rows.sort((a, b) => d3.descending(a.value ?? a.estimate_p0 ?? 0, b.value ?? b.estimate_p0 ?? 0));
          return rows;
        }
        function renderTable(vals) {
          // the table view is usually hidden; building 7,069 rows on every repaint would
          // cost more than the map does
          if (tableWrap.hidden) { tableStale = true; return; }
          tableStale = false;
          const rows = buildRows(vals);
          const cols = Object.keys(rows[0] || { code: "", name: "" });
          table.querySelector("thead").innerHTML =
            `<tr>${cols.map((c) => `<th>${c.replace(/_/g, " ")}</th>`).join("")}</tr>`;
          table.querySelector("tbody").innerHTML = rows.slice(0, 300).map((r) =>
            `<tr>${cols.map((c) => `<td>${typeof r[c] === "number" ? fmt2(r[c]) : (r[c] ?? "—")}</td>`).join("")}</tr>`).join("");
        }
        document.querySelectorAll("#view-seg button").forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => {
          document.querySelectorAll("#view-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
          const isTable = b.dataset.view === "table";
          tableWrap.hidden = !isTable;
          document.querySelector(".map-shell").hidden = isTable;
          if (isTable && tableStale) renderTable(valuesFor());
        }));
        document.getElementById("dl-csv").addEventListener("click", () => {
          const dlRows = buildRows(valuesFor());
          if (!dlRows.length) return;
          const cols = Object.keys(dlRows[0]);
          const csv = [cols.join(",")].concat(dlRows.map((r) =>
            cols.map((c) => {
              const v = r[c];
              return v == null ? "" : typeof v === "string" && /[",]/.test(v) ? `"${v.replace(/"/g, '""')}"` : v;
            }).join(","))).join("\n");
          const a = document.createElement("a");
          a.href = URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv], { type: "text/csv" }));
          a.download = `poverty-map_${state.level}_${state.metric}_${state.year}.csv`;
          a.click();
          setTimeout(() => URL.revokeObjectURL(a.href), 2000);
        });

        /* ---- URL state on load ---- */
        const h = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1));
        if (h.get("y") && YEARS.includes(+h.get("y"))) {
          state.year = +h.get("y");
          yearRange.value = String(YEARS.indexOf(state.year));
          yearOut.textContent = String(state.year);
        }
        if (h.get("m") && METRIC[h.get("m")]) {
          state.metric = h.get("m");
          document.querySelectorAll("#metric-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x.dataset.metric === state.metric));
        }
        if (h.get("l") === "adm3" && estimates) {
          document.querySelectorAll("#lvl-seg button").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x.dataset.lvl === "adm3"));
          setLevel("adm3").then(() => { const c = h.get("c"); if (c) { const i = currentLayer.index.get(c); if (i != null) openPanel(currentLayer.units[i]); } });
        } else if (h.get("c")) {
          const i = ADM2.index.get(h.get("c"));
          if (i != null) setTimeout(() => openPanel(ADM2.units[i]), 60);
        }
        addEventListener("hashchange", () => {
          const q = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1));
          const c = q.get("c");
          if (c && c !== state.code) {
            const i = currentLayer.index.get(c);
            if (i != null) openPanel(currentLayer.units[i]);
          }
        });
      });

      /* ══════════════════════════ METHOD ══════════════════════════════════════════ */
      sect("method", () => {
        const cl = document.getElementById("caveat-list");
        const caveats = statsJson?.caveats ?? [
          "Kecamatan values are model estimates that distribute the official regency rate; they are not survey measurements.",
          "Open Buildings is a single 2023 vintage and ESA WorldCover a single 2021 vintage — only night lights and population vary year to year.",
          "Susenas and DHS microdata are restricted, so the target is the published regency poverty rate rather than household consumption.",
        ];
        cl.innerHTML = caveats.map((c) => `<li>${c}</li>`).join("");

        if (recon) {
          document.getElementById("recon-summary").innerHTML =
            `COD-AB carries <b>${recon.codab_adm2}</b> ADM2 polygons on a 2020-04 vintage; BPS publishes ` +
            `<b>${recon.matched}</b> kabupaten/kota to ${LATEST}. <b>${recon.by_pcode}</b> join directly on the ` +
            `P-code digits. The remaining <b>${recon.by_name}</b> are the post-2020 <i>pemekaran</i> — the Papua ` +
            `province splits, where the same regency was re-coded from 91xx/94xx to 92xx and 95xx–97xx — and are ` +
            `resolved by name, one-to-one, against the unmatched set only. <b>${recon.non_census}</b> COD-AB ` +
            `polygons are lakes, a reservoir and a forest block: they are not census units and get no estimate. ` +
            `<b>${(recon.unresolved || []).length}</b> codes remain unresolved` +
            ((recon.unresolved || []).length ? ", and they are listed below." : " — every published regency has geometry.");
          const rows = (recon.rows || []).filter((r) => r.resolution !== "non-census polygon");
          const t = document.getElementById("recon-table");
          t.querySelector("thead").innerHTML =
            "<tr><th>COD-AB 2020</th><th>Name</th><th>BPS current</th><th>Resolution</th></tr>";
          t.querySelector("tbody").innerHTML = rows.map((r) => `
            <tr class="${String(r.resolution).startsWith("UNMATCHED") || r.resolution === "ambiguous" ? "bad" : ""}">
              <td>${r.codab_code || "—"}</td><td>${r.codab_name || r.bps_name || "—"}</td>
              <td>${r.bps_code || "—"}</td><td>${r.resolution}</td></tr>`).join("");
        }

        const ml = document.getElementById("manifest-list");
        ml.innerHTML = Object.entries(manifest).filter(([, v]) => v && typeof v === "object" && v.status)
          .map(([k, v]) => `<li><code>${k}</code> — ${v.status}${v.bytes ? ` · ${(v.bytes / 1024).toFixed(0)} kB` : ""}${v.units ? ` · ${fmtI(v.units)} units` : ""}${v.res_m ? ` · ${v.res_m} m lattice` : ""}${v.waiting_on ? ` · waiting on ${v.waiting_on.join(", ")}` : ""}</li>`).join("");
      });
    </script>

